{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011chP62NHT9QmrWpmss6VUW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-10-12 19:00 +07\n2\t# Task: apply codex's r4 findings to the simple discovery-order note (targeted, small)\n3\tYou are claude-fable-5-1, NEW session. Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-numbering`, branch `numbering-note`. Edit ONLY `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md`, `collab/numbering-probe`, and your report `collab/1792240000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-revise4.report.md`. No git add/commit. Vocabulary per UCF 7.5.3. Read codex's findings `collab/1792230000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review-r4.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md` (no canonicality counterexample in 5,000 states; the changes are resource gates, decoder order and wording). Apply all six findings:\n4\t1. HIGH depth: enforce the structural `:depth` gate BEFORE any recursive scan (occurrence counts, memo-key hashing, spelling preparation, literal/descriptor representation sizing), by carrying depth through the scans or using a bounded iterative traversal; add the adversarial case (one reachable cell inside 3,000 nested vectors with `{:depth 3}` must refuse `[:depth]`, not overflow the stack) to the note's acceptance list and the probe.\n5\t2. MEDIUM `rep-bound`: restore a remaining-budget-aware, early-aborting estimator (like 6a's `size` with its `remaining` argument and intermediate limit checks); the 400,000-scalar literal in a set under `{:work 2000}` must refuse after a bounded number of estimator steps, not 400,012; qualify the accounting claim: encoded bytes vs representation nodes vs actual heap, the bound is a conservative abstract charge.\n6\t3. MEDIUM decoder order: fix the probe's wrapper so discovery recomputation runs BEFORE frame validation (as the production insertion at rows 570-575 will) and make `numbering-precedes-frame-defect` really test it; keep the note's statement that production code preserves the placement.\n7\t4. LOW stale example at note 270-274: replace with equal-size, equal-degree unresolved incidence structures or remove.\n8\t5. LOW termination measure: make it precise for the queue (multiset measure on pending subtree sizes plus unnumbered-cell count plus explicit phase transitions), or restrict the no-cell-numbered tie branch to invalid duplicate values and state the premise.\n9\t6. LOW owner summary and note: do not say \"the rest were harmless ties\"; say 470 exhaustively harmless, 100 demonstrably non-interchangeable, 320 sampled-equal and undecided (use codex's table), plus the 0.95% / 2% / 17.8% rates as generator rates only.\n10\tRerun the independent generator (the corrected script is in codex's r3 findings) and your own search; report counts; confirm 0 invariance failures. Foreground only. Report: 15 lines plain summary, then findings status, ending READY or NOT READY for an implementation brief.\n11\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"704437a3-7e24-494b-ab26-b13fa72d3d40","uuid":"6e0cffdd-f9e2-426a-91ea-de971d4fa6ea","timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:43:05.522Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-numbering/collab/1792240000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-revise4.prompt.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-12 19:00 +07\n# Task: apply codex's r4 findings to the simple discovery-order note (targeted, small)\nYou are claude-fable-5-1, NEW session. Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-numbering`, branch `numbering-note`. Edit ONLY `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md`, `collab/numbering-probe`, and your report `collab/1792240000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-revise4.report.md`. No git add/commit. Vocabulary per UCF 7.5.3. Read codex's findings `collab/1792230000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review-r4.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md` (no canonicality counterexample in 5,000 states; the changes are resource gates, decoder order and wording). Apply all six findings:\n1. HIGH depth: enforce the structural `:depth` gate BEFORE any recursive scan (occurrence counts, memo-key hashing, spelling preparation, literal/descriptor representation sizing), by carrying depth through the scans or using a bounded iterative traversal; add the adversarial case (one reachable cell inside 3,000 nested vectors with `{:depth 3}` must refuse `[:depth]`, not overflow the stack) to the note's acceptance list and the probe.\n2. MEDIUM `rep-bound`: restore a remaining-budget-aware, early-aborting estimator (like 6a's `size` with its `remaining` argument and intermediate limit checks); the 400,000-scalar literal in a set under `{:work 2000}` must refuse after a bounded number of estimator steps, not 400,012; qualify the accounting claim: encoded bytes vs representation nodes vs actual heap, the bound is a conservative abstract charge.\n3. MEDIUM decoder order: fix the probe's wrapper so discovery recomputation runs BEFORE frame validation (as the production insertion at rows 570-575 will) and make `numbering-precedes-frame-defect` really test it; keep the note's statement that production code preserves the placement.\n4. LOW stale example at note 270-274: replace with equal-size, equal-degree unresolved incidence structures or remove.\n5. LOW termination measure: make it precise for the queue (multiset measure on pending subtree sizes plus unnumbered-cell count plus explicit phase transitions), or restrict the no-cell-numbered tie branch to invalid duplicate values and state the premise.\n6. LOW owner summary and note: do not say \"the rest were harmless ties\"; say 470 exhaustively harmless, 100 demonstrably non-interchangeable, 320 sampled-equal and undecided (use codex's table), plus the 0.95% / 2% / 17.8% rates as generator rates only.\nRerun the independent generator (the corrected script is in codex's r3 findings) and your own search; report counts; confirm 0 invariance failures. Foreground only. Report: 15 lines plain summary, then findings status, ending READY or NOT READY for an implementation brief.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011chP62NHT9QmrWpmss6VUW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
