{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TFxocCt4ZC7ELk5Sev1rNh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns probe.discovery\n2\t  \"Prototype of discovery-order cursor-cell numbering, the BASE design of the\n3\t   note of 2026-10-12 (round 4), over the 6a abstract task representation\n4\t   (yin.vm.ucf.rows). Not repo code; a scratch project under collab/. The\n5\t   round-3 variants (components, residue search) live in probe.discovery-r3.\n6\t\n7\t   Vocabulary: UCF 7.5.3. A cursor cell is the VM box the carrier serializes;\n8\t   its source id is the lift's local name; the procedure assigns :yin.k/cc-n.\n9\t\n10\t   The rule. A cursor cell gets the next number the first time the walk meets\n11\t   it. The walk is pre-order over the task in table order. A guest :set or\n12\t   :map is turned into a vector of its members (a map entry as [:entry k v])\n13\t   sorted by KEY: the spelling of a local walk over the member under the\n14\t   current numbering, with numbered cells spelled by number and unnumbered\n15\t   ones by local first-occurrence index, body rank and occurrence count.\n16\t   Members whose keys tie are POSTPONED to the run's queue and re-keyed after\n17\t   the rest of the walk, until a pass numbers nothing. A remaining tie group\n18\t   is entered in listed order when the TIE TEST holds (common key complete;\n19\t   the members' unnumbered cells pairwise disjoint and occurring in no member\n20\t   of another remaining group); otherwise the root walk refuses\n21\t   :yin.k/non-portable :unresolved-cursor-cells and a key walk spells the\n22\t   group as [:tie K ... K] in its key.\n23\t\n24\t   Budgets: :cursor-cells (census size, first), :depth (nesting of the walk),\n25\t   :work (one unit per position visited or spelled, plus 6a's representation\n26\t   bound of every value before it is CBOR-encoded for a comparison). Exceeding\n27\t   one is :yin.k/unsupported :resource-limit, never a canonicality verdict.\n28\t\n29\t   Diagnostic switches (*numbering-opts*): :permissive enters a failing group\n30\t   in listed order instead of refusing (used to test interchangeability by\n31\t   exhaustion or sampling); :count-spelling false drops the occurrence count\n32\t   from the key (the owner's literal direction, for measurement).\"\n33\t  (:require [clojure.set :as set]\n34\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n35\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n36\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n37\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-test :as rt]\n38\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]))\n39\t\n40\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- schema\n41\t\n42\t(def synthetic-table\n43\t  \"The one row that exists only inside the procedure: a :map entry as an\n44\t   ordered pair, so the alias pattern across key and value is in its key.\"\n45\t  {:entry [:V :V]})\n46\t\n47\t(defn descriptors [kind slots]\n48\t  (let [schema (or (get rows/row-table kind) (get synthetic-table kind))]\n49\t    (cond (= schema :pending) (into [:D] (get rows/pending-table (first slots)))\n50\t          (= :repeat (first schema)) (vec (repeat (count slots) (second schema)))\n51\t          (= :pairs (first schema)) (vec (take (count slots) (cycle (rest schema))))\n52\t          :else schema)))\n53\t\n54\t(defn ref? [d] (and (vector? d) (= :ref (first d))))\n55\t(defn refs? [d] (and (vector? d) (= :refs (first d))))\n56\t(defn v? [d] (contains? #{:V :optional-V} d))\n57\t\n58\t(defn bytes-key\n59\t  \"Uncharged encoding; generators and diagnostics only.\"\n60\t  [x] (mapv #(bit-and (int %) 255) (seq (cbor/encode x))))\n61\t\n62\t(defn compare-bytes [a b]\n63\t  (loop [i 0]\n64\t    (cond (= i (count a)) (if (= i (count b)) 0 -1)\n65\t          (= i (count b)) 1\n66\t          (= (nth a i) (nth b i)) (recur (inc i))\n67\t          :else (compare (nth a i) (nth b i)))))\n68\t\n69\t(def keyed-structural #{:bindings :store :parked-table})\n70\t\n71\t(defn elem-item\n72\t  \"The item a member is keyed and entered as: a :set member is its V; a :map\n73\t   entry [k v] is the synthetic ordered row [:entry k v].\"\n74\t  [kind e]\n75\t  (if (= :map kind) [:row {:kind :entry :slots (vec e)}] e))\n76\t\n77\t(defn child-task? [ctx n] (and (= :task (:kind n)) (not (identical? n (:task ctx)))))\n78\t\n79\t;; --------------------------------------------------------------- budgets\n80\t\n81\t(def default-budget\n82\t  \"6a's budget without :label-bytes and :search; :work now also counts\n83\t   representation bytes, so its default takes over :label-bytes' scale.\"\n84\t  (assoc (dissoc rows/default-budget :label-bytes :search) :work 4194304))\n85\t\n86\t(defn- limit! [category]\n87\t  (throw (ex-info \"resource limit\"\n88\t                  {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :resource-limit :yin.k/path [category]})))\n89\t\n90\t(defn- spend! [ctx category amount]\n91\t  (let [n (get (swap! (:counter ctx) update category (fnil + 0) amount) category)]\n92\t    (when (> n (get (:budget ctx) category)) (limit! category))))\n93\t\n94\t(defn- rep-bound\n95\t  \"6a's conservative representation bound (check-label-bytes!): an upper\n96\t   bound of the CBOR bytes of x, computed by reading x and allocating nothing.\"\n97\t  [x]\n98\t  (let [n (cond (cbor/byte-payload? x) (+ 16 (alength ^bytes x))\n99\t                (string? x) (+ 128 (* 4 (count x)))\n100\t                (or (keyword? x) (symbol? x)) (+ 128 (* 4 (count (str x))))\n101\t                (coll? x) (reduce (fn [t v] (+ t (rep-bound v))) 128 (if (map? x) (mapcat identity x) x))\n102\t                :else 128)]\n103\t    (if (meta x) (+ n (rep-bound (meta x))) n)))\n104\t\n105\t(defn- key-bytes!\n106\t  \"Charge the representation bound of x to :work, then encode x for comparison.\n107\t   Every encoding the procedure makes goes through here.\"\n108\t  [ctx x]\n109\t  (spend! ctx :work (rep-bound x))\n110\t  (let [bs (bytes-key x)]\n111\t    (swap! (:counter ctx) update :encoded-bytes (fnil + 0) (count bs))\n112\t    bs))\n113\t\n114\t(defn- sort-by-key!\n115\t  \"xs in the bytewise order of (f x), each encoded once (stable).\"\n116\t  [ctx f xs]\n117\t  (mapv second (sort #(compare-bytes (first %1) (first %2)) (mapv (fn [x] [(key-bytes! ctx (f x)) x]) xs))))\n118\t\n119\t;; ------------------------------------------------------------ cell scans\n120\t\n121\t(defn- walk-cells\n122\t  \"Call f on every cursor cell at a position under slot (d x); census and\n123\t   install children excluded; one :work unit per position.\"\n124\t  [ctx d x f]\n125\t  (letfn [(slot [d x]\n126\t            (spend! ctx :work 1)\n127\t            (cond (ref? d) (node x)\n128\t                  (refs? d) (run! node x)\n129\t                  (= :C d) (f x)\n130\t                  (v? d) (when x (case (first x) :cursor-cell (f (second x)) :row (node (second x)) nil))\n131\t                  :else nil))\n132\t          (node [n]\n133\t            (when-not (or (= :cursor-cells (:kind n)) (child-task? ctx n))\n134\t              (dorun (map slot (descriptors (:kind n) (:slots n)) (:slots n)))))]\n135\t    (slot d x)))\n136\t\n137\t(defn item-cells\n138\t  \"The cursor cells under slot (d x), memoized per procedure on the slot value.\"\n139\t  [ctx d x]\n140\t  (or (get @(:cells-memo ctx) [d x])\n141\t      (let [acc (atom #{})]\n142\t        (walk-cells ctx d x #(swap! acc conj %))\n143\t        (swap! (:cells-memo ctx) assoc [d x] @acc)\n144\t        @acc)))\n145\t\n146\t(defn- occurrence-counts\n147\t  \"Cursor cell -> number of positions of the task holding it.\"\n148\t  [ctx task]\n149\t  (let [acc (atom {})]\n150\t    (walk-cells ctx [:ref :task] task #(swap! acc update % (fnil inc 0)))\n151\t    @acc))\n152\t\n153\t(defn body-label [body]\n154\t  (let [[stream position] (:slots body)]\n155\t    [:body (into [:stream] (:slots stream)) position]))\n156\t\n157\t(defn- body-ranks\n158\t  \"Cursor cell -> rank of its body label among the census's distinct body\n159\t   labels in bytewise order (rank order = label order, so keys stay\n160\t   independent of the descriptor's size).\"\n161\t  [ctx bodies]\n162\t  (let [labels (into {} (map (fn [[c b]] [c (body-label b)])) bodies)\n163\t        ranks (into {} (map-indexed (fn [i l] [l i])) (sort-by-key! ctx identity (distinct (vals labels))))]\n164\t    (into {} (map (fn [[c l]] [c (get ranks l)])) labels)))\n165\t\n166\t;; ------------------------------------------------------------------ runs\n167\t\n168\t(def ^:dynamic *trace* false)\n169\t\n170\t(defn- new-run [ctx num tag next]\n171\t  {:ctx ctx :num (atom num) :tag tag :next (atom next) :groups (atom []) :gid (atom 0) :refused (atom nil)})\n172\t\n173\t(defn- meet!\n174\t  \"W2. A cursor cell met for the first time receives the run's next number.\"\n175\t  [run c]\n176\t  (when-not (contains? @(:num run) c)\n177\t    (let [k @(:next run)]\n178\t      (swap! (:num run) assoc c [(:tag run) k])\n179\t      (swap! (:next run) inc)\n180\t      true)))\n181\t\n182\t(declare enter-node! unordered! local-run spell-slot spell-node)\n183\t\n184\t(defn- enter-slot! [run d x path]\n185\t  (let [ctx (:ctx run)]\n186\t    (spend! ctx :work 1)\n187\t    (when (> (count path) (get (:budget ctx) :depth)) (limit! :depth))\n188\t    (cond (ref? d) (enter-node! run x path)\n189\t          (refs? d) (dorun (map-indexed (fn [i n] (enter-node! run n (conj path i))) x))\n190\t          (= :C d) (meet! run x)\n191\t          (v? d) (when x (case (first x)\n192\t                           :cursor-cell (meet! run (second x))\n193\t                           :row (enter-node! run (second x) path)\n194\t                           nil))\n195\t          :else nil)))\n196\t\n197\t(defn- enter-node!\n198\t  \"W1. Pre-order: table order for slots; ordered repeated slots in order;\n199\t   keyed structural rows in the byte order of the key; :window in register\n200\t   order; installs and module stores by name; :set and :map by keys with\n201\t   ties postponed; census and children not entered.\"\n202\t  [run n path]\n203\t  (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n ctx (:ctx run) ds (descriptors kind slots)]\n204\t    (cond\n205\t      (= :cursor-cells kind) nil\n206\t      (child-task? ctx n) nil\n207\t      (= :task kind)\n208\t      (doseq [[i d x] (map vector (range) ds slots)]\n209\t        (if (contains? #{7 12} i)\n210\t          (doseq [child (sort-by-key! ctx #(first (:slots %)) x)]\n211\t            (enter-node! run child (conj path i (first (:slots child)))))\n212\t          (enter-slot! run d x (conj path i))))\n213\t      (contains? keyed-structural kind)\n214\t      (doseq [[k v] (sort-by-key! ctx first (partition 2 slots))]\n215\t        (enter-slot! run (second ds) v (conj path k)))\n216\t      (= :window kind)\n217\t      (doseq [[r v] (sort-by first (partition 2 slots))] (enter-slot! run :V v (conj path r)))\n218\t      (= :set kind) (unordered! run n :set (vec slots) path)\n219\t      (= :map kind) (unordered! run n :map (mapv vec (partition 2 slots)) path)\n220\t      :else (dorun (map-indexed (fn [i [d x]] (enter-slot! run d x (conj path i))) (map vector ds slots))))))\n221\t\n222\t(defn- unordered!\n223\t  \"The transformation: key every member by a local walk under the numbering\n224\t   at this moment; members with a unique key are entered in key order; a run\n225\t   of equal keys is one tie group, postponed to the run's queue (postponement\n226\t   order: containers in walk order, groups within a container in key order).\n227\t   A member's path is the container's path plus :member (there is no\n228\t   canonical index into an unordered container); a group remembers its\n229\t   container by identity.\"\n230\t  [run container kind elems path]\n231\t  (let [keyed (mapv (fn [e] [(local-run run (elem-item kind e) (conj path :member)) e]) elems)\n232\t        groups (partition-by (comp :bytes first) (sort #(compare-bytes (:bytes (first %1)) (:bytes (first %2))) keyed))]\n233\t    (when (and *trace* (= :n (:tag run)))\n234\t      (println \"  [sort]\" path \"num\" @(:num run))\n235\t      (doseq [g groups] (println \"    \" (if (= 1 (count g)) \"enter\" \"POSTPONE\") (mapv (fn [[r e]] [e (:spell r)]) g))))\n236\t    (doseq [g groups]\n237\t      (if (= 1 (count g))\n238\t        (enter-slot! run :V (elem-item kind (second (first g))) (conj path :member))\n239\t        (swap! (:groups run) conj {:id (swap! (:gid run) inc) :container container :kind kind :path path\n240\t                                   :key (:spell (first (first g))) :complete? (:complete? (first (first g)))\n241\t                                   :elems (mapv second g)})))))\n242\t\n243\t(defn- fixpoint!\n244\t  \"W3. Re-examine every postponed group in order under the current numbering;\n245\t   repeat while a pass numbers a cursor cell and groups remain.\"\n246\t  [run]\n247\t  (loop []\n248\t    (let [before (count @(:num run)) groups @(:groups run)]\n249\t      (reset! (:groups run) [])\n250\t      (doseq [{:keys [container kind elems path]} groups] (unordered! run container kind elems path))\n251\t      (when (and (seq @(:groups run)) (> (count @(:num run)) before)) (recur)))))\n252\t\n253\t(defn- unnumbered-cells [run kind e]\n254\t  (let [num @(:num run)]\n255\t    (set (remove #(contains? num %) (item-cells (:ctx run) :V (elem-item kind e))))))\n256\t\n257\t(defn- group-failure\n258\t  \"T, the tie test. nil when the group's members are interchangeable: the\n259\t   common key is complete, and the members' unnumbered cursor cells are\n260\t   pairwise disjoint and occur in no member of another remaining group.\n261\t   Otherwise the reason.\"\n262\t  [run groups g]\n263\t  (let [own (mapv #(unnumbered-cells run (:kind g) %) (:elems g))\n264\t        others (reduce into #{} (for [h groups :when (not= (:id h) (:id g)) e (:elems h)]\n265\t                                  (unnumbered-cells run (:kind h) e)))]\n266\t    (cond (not (:complete? g)) :incomplete-key\n267\t          (not= (reduce + (map count own)) (count (reduce into #{} own))) :shared-within-group\n268\t          (some #(seq (set/intersection % others)) own) :shared-across-groups\n269\t          :else nil)))\n270\t\n271\t(defn- resolve!\n272\t  \"Postponed groups to completion: fixpoint, then the tie test on every\n273\t   remaining group; all pass: enter them in listed order and repeat; any\n274\t   fails: the root run refuses, a key run leaves them as residue.\"\n275\t  [run]\n276\t  (loop []\n277\t    (fixpoint! run)\n278\t    (let [groups @(:groups run) ctx (:ctx run)]\n279\t      (when (seq groups)\n280\t        (let [failing (vec (keep (fn [g] (when-let [why (group-failure run groups g)] (assoc g :why why))) groups))]\n281\t          (when (and *trace* (= :n (:tag run)))\n282\t            (println \"  [ties]\" (mapv (fn [g] [(:id g) (:path g) (:elems g) (:why g)]) (map #(assoc % :why (group-failure run groups %)) groups))))\n283\t          (cond\n284\t            (empty? failing)\n285\t            ;; Interchangeable groups are independent of each other (their\n286\t            ;; cells are confined), so all are entered before the next pass.\n287\t            (do (reset! (:groups run) [])\n288\t                (doseq [g groups e (:elems g)] (enter-slot! run :V (elem-item (:kind g) e) (conj (:path g) :member)))\n289\t                (recur))\n290\t            (:permissive ctx)\n291\t            ;; Diagnostic only: enter the first group in listed order, then\n292\t            ;; re-key the rest (what an unsound \"equal keys, host order\" rule does).\n293\t            (do (reset! (:groups run) (vec (rest groups)))\n294\t                (doseq [e (:elems (first groups))] (enter-slot! run :V (elem-item (:kind (first groups)) e) (conj (:path (first groups)) :member)))\n295\t                (recur))\n296\t            (= :n (:tag run))\n297\t            (reset! (:refused run)\n298\t                    {:kind :unresolved-cursor-cells\n299\t                     :path (:path (first failing))\n300\t                     :why (mapv :why failing)\n301\t                     :cursor-cells (vec (sort (distinct (mapcat (fn [g] (mapcat #(unnumbered-cells run (:kind g) %) (:elems g))) failing))))})\n302\t            :else nil))))))\n303\t\n304\t(defn- local-run\n305\t  \"A key walk: the same procedure on one member from the enclosing run's\n306\t   numbering, tag :u; its result is the member's key (spelling under its\n307\t   final numbering, residue spelled [:tie K ...]) and whether it is complete.\n308\t   Memoized on (item, numbering restricted to the item's cells, counter).\"\n309\t  [run item path]\n310\t  (let [ctx (:ctx run)\n311\t        cells (item-cells ctx :V item)\n312\t        num @(:num run)\n313\t        start (if (= :u (:tag run)) @(:next run) 0)\n314\t        mk [item (select-keys num cells) start]]\n315\t    (or (get @(:memo ctx) mk)\n316\t        (let [sub (new-run ctx num :u start)]\n317\t          (spend! ctx :work (count cells))\n318\t          (enter-slot! sub :V item path)\n319\t          (resolve! sub)\n320\t          (let [spell (spell-slot sub :V item path)\n321\t                r {:spell spell :bytes (key-bytes! ctx spell) :complete? (empty? @(:groups sub))}]\n322\t            (swap! (:counter ctx) update :local-runs (fnil + 0) 1)\n323\t            (swap! (:memo ctx) assoc mk r)\n324\t            r)))))\n325\t\n326\t;; -------------------------------------------------------------- spelling\n327\t\n328\t(defn- spell-cell [run c]\n329\t  (let [[t k] (get @(:num run) c) ctx (:ctx run)]\n330\t    (case t\n331\t      :n [:cursor-cell [:n k]]\n332\t      :u [:cursor-cell (if (:count-spelling ctx)\n333\t                         [:u k (get (:ranks ctx) c) (get (:counts ctx) c)]\n334\t                         [:u k (get (:ranks ctx) c)])]\n335\t      (throw (ex-info \"spelling an unnumbered cursor cell\" {:cursor-cell c})))))\n336\t\n337\t(defn- spell-slot [run d x path]\n338\t  (spend! (:ctx run) :work 1)\n339\t  (cond (ref? d) (spell-node run x path)\n340\t        (refs? d) (vec (map-indexed (fn [i n] (spell-node run n (conj path i))) x))\n341\t        (= :C d) (spell-cell run x)\n342\t        (v? d) (if (nil? x) x\n343\t                   (case (first x)\n344\t                     :cursor-cell (spell-cell run (second x))\n345\t                     :row [:row (spell-node run (second x) path)]\n346\t                     x))\n347\t        :else x))\n348\t\n349\t(defn- spell-node\n350\t  \"The spelling of a row under the run's final numbering: literals and\n351\t   structural data as themselves (by reference), rows expanded in place,\n352\t   keyed rows in key order, a :set or :map as the sorted vector of its\n353\t   members' spellings with each surviving tie group as [:tie K ...].\"\n354\t  [run n path]\n355\t  (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n ctx (:ctx run) ds (descriptors kind slots)]\n356\t    (cond\n357\t      (= :cursor-cells kind) [:cursor-cells]\n358\t      (child-task? ctx n) [:child]\n359\t      (= :task kind)\n360\t      (into [kind]\n361\t            (map-indexed (fn [i [d x]]\n362\t                           (if (contains? #{7 12} i)\n363\t                             (sort-by-key! ctx #(nth % 1) (mapv #(spell-node run % (conj path i (first (:slots %)))) x))\n364\t                             (spell-slot run d x (conj path i))))\n365\t                         (map vector ds slots)))\n366\t      (contains? keyed-structural kind)\n367\t      (into [kind] (mapcat identity (sort-by-key! ctx first\n368\t                                                  (mapv (fn [[k v]] [k (spell-slot run (second ds) v (conj path k))])\n369\t                                                        (partition 2 slots)))))\n370\t      (= :window kind)\n371\t      (into [kind] (mapcat (fn [[r v]] [r (spell-slot run :V v (conj path r))]) (sort-by first (partition 2 slots))))\n372\t      (contains? #{:set :map} kind)\n373\t      (let [elems (if (= :set kind) (vec slots) (mapv vec (partition 2 slots)))\n374\t            tied (filter #(identical? n (:container %)) @(:groups run))\n375\t            tied-elems (set (mapcat :elems tied))\n376\t            plain (keep (fn [e] (when-not (tied-elems e) (spell-slot run :V (elem-item kind e) (conj path :member)))) elems)\n377\t            ties (map #(into [:tie] (repeat (count (:elems %)) (:key %))) tied)]\n378\t        (into [kind] (sort-by-key! ctx identity (concat plain ties))))\n379\t      :else (into [kind] (map-indexed (fn [i [d x]] (spell-slot run d x (conj path i))) (map vector ds slots))))))\n380\t\n381\t;; ------------------------------------------------------------- procedure\n382\t\n383\t(def ^:dynamic *numbering-opts*\n384\t  \"Options for every run of the procedure in scope (root and install\n385\t   children): :permissive, :count-spelling, :budget.\"\n386\t  {})\n387\t\n388\t(defn discovery-numbering\n389\t  \"Returns {:numbering {src -> :yin.k/cc-n} :used {...}} or {:refused {...}}.\n390\t   Throws :resource-limit when a budget is exceeded, and a defect (never a\n391\t   refusal) when the numbering is not total.\"\n392\t  ([task] (discovery-numbering task *numbering-opts*))\n393\t  ([task opts]\n394\t   (let [census (nth (:slots task) 9)\n395\t         bodies (into {} (map vec) (partition 2 (:slots census)))\n396\t         ctx {:task task :bodies bodies\n397\t              :memo (atom {}) :cells-memo (atom {})\n398\t              :budget (merge default-budget (:budget opts))\n399\t              :counter (atom {})\n400\t              :permissive (:permissive opts)\n401\t              :count-spelling (not= false (:count-spelling opts))}\n402\t         _ (spend! ctx :cursor-cells (count bodies))\n403\t         ctx (assoc ctx :ranks (body-ranks ctx bodies) :counts (occurrence-counts ctx task))\n404\t         run (new-run ctx {} :n 1)]\n405\t     (enter-node! run task [])\n406\t     (resolve! run)\n407\t     (if-let [r @(:refused run)]\n408\t       {:refused r :used @(:counter ctx)}\n409\t       (let [numbered (set (keys @(:num run))) declared (set (keys bodies))]\n410\t         (when (seq @(:groups run)) (throw (ex-info \"residue after resolve\" {})))\n411\t         (when (not= numbered declared)\n412\t           (throw (ex-info \"numbering is not total\" {:missing (vec (sort (remove numbered declared)))\n413\t                                                      :extra (vec (sort (remove declared numbered)))})))\n414\t         {:numbering (into {} (map (fn [[c [_ k]]] [c (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"cc-\" k))])) @(:num run))\n415\t          :used @(:counter ctx)})))))\n416\t\n417\t;; --------------------------------------------------------------- emission\n418\t;; 6a's emit-node with install children numbered by discovery order and a\n419\t;; row path threaded for the child refusal.\n420\t\n421\t(def ^:private ordered-slots @#'rows/ordered-slots)\n422\t(def ^:private check-literal-markers! @#'rows/check-literal-markers!)\n423\t(def ^:private byte-compare @#'rows/byte-compare)\n424\t\n425\t(declare emit-node*)\n426\t\n427\t(defn- refuse-unresolved! [r path]\n428\t  (throw (ex-info \"unresolved cursor cells\"\n429\t                  {:yin.k/status :yin.k/non-portable :yin.k/kind :unresolved-cursor-cells\n430\t                   :yin.k/path (into path (:path r)) :yin.k/cursor-cells (:cursor-cells r)\n431\t                   ;; probe-only diagnostic, not part of the refusal's contract\n432\t                   :probe/why (:why r)})))\n433\t\n434\t(defn- emit-slot* [d x numbering rows path]\n435\t  (when-not (or (ref? d) (refs? d) (= :C d))\n436\t    (check-literal-markers! (if (v? d) (when (= :lit (first x)) (second x)) x)))\n437\t  (cond\n438\t    (ref? d) (emit-node* x numbering rows path)\n439\t    (refs? d) (reduce (fn [[out rs] [j n]]\n440\t                        (let [p (conj path (if (= :install (:kind n)) (first (:slots n)) j))\n441\t                              [id rs'] (emit-node* n numbering rs p)]\n442\t                          [(conj out id) rs']))\n443\t                      [[] rows] (map-indexed vector x))\n444\t    (= d :C) [(get numbering x x) rows]\n445\t    (v? d) (case (first x)\n446\t             :row (let [[id rs] (emit-node* (second x) numbering rows path)] [[:row id] rs])\n447\t             :cursor-cell [[:cursor-cell (get numbering (second x) (second x))] rows]\n448\t             [x rows])\n449\t    :else [x rows]))\n450\t\n451\t(defn- emit-node* [n numbering rows path]\n452\t  (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n\n453\t        [slots rows] (reduce (fn [[out rs] [i d x]]\n454\t                               (if (and (ref? d) (= :task (:kind x)))\n455\t                                 (let [r (discovery-numbering x)\n456\t                                       _ (when (:refused r) (refuse-unresolved! (:refused r) path))\n457\t                                       [id child-rows] (emit-node* x (:numbering r) {} [])]\n458\t                                   [(conj out id) (merge rs child-rows)])\n459\t                                 (let [[x' rs'] (emit-slot* d x numbering rs (conj path i))] [(conj out x') rs'])))\n460\t                             [[] rows] (map vector (range) (descriptors kind slots) slots))\n461\t        slots (if (= kind :task)\n462\t                (-> slots\n463\t                    (update 7 #(vec (sort (fn [a b] (byte-compare (nth (get rows a) 2) (nth (get rows b) 2))) %)))\n464\t                    (update 12 #(vec (sort (fn [a b] (byte-compare (nth (get rows a) 2) (nth (get rows b) 2))) %))))\n465\t                (ordered-slots kind slots))\n466\t        body (into [kind] slots) id (jing/segment-key body)]\n467\t    [id (assoc rows id (into [id] body))]))\n468\t\n469\t(defn emit*\n470\t  \"Lift side: number by discovery order, emit; refuses :yin.k/non-portable\n471\t   :unresolved-cursor-cells for the root or for any install child (path\n472\t   [12 <name> ...]); a budget refusal propagates as itself.\"\n473\t  [task]\n474\t  (let [r (discovery-numbering task)]\n475\t    (when (:refused r) (refuse-unresolved! (:refused r) []))\n476\t    (let [[id rows] (emit-node* task (:numbering r) {} [])]\n477\t      {:yin.k/handoff true :yin.k/version 3 :yin.k/root id :yin.k/rows (vec (vals rows))})))\n478\t\n479\t(defn decode*\n480\t  \"Receiver side: 6a's decode* with its own numbering check off (it still\n481\t   runs 6a's recompute under 6a's budget: a probe limitation), then the whole\n482\t   discovery recomputation (root and install children) under one\n483\t   translation: only a lift-side :yin.k/non-portable of kind\n484\t   :unresolved-cursor-cells becomes :yin.k/undecodable\n485\t   :unresolved-cursor-cells with the path prefixed by the carried root id;\n486\t   anything else (a resource refusal) propagates as itself.\"\n487\t  [wire]\n488\t  (let [task (@#'rows/decode* wire (assoc rows/default-budget :check-numbering false))\n489\t        root (:yin.k/root wire)\n490\t        id (try (:yin.k/root (emit* task))\n491\t                (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n492\t                  (let [d (ex-data e)]\n493\t                    (if (and (= :yin.k/non-portable (:yin.k/status d)) (= :unresolved-cursor-cells (:yin.k/kind d)))\n494\t                      (throw (ex-info \"unresolved cursor cells\"\n495\t                                      (assoc d :yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/path (into [root] (:yin.k/path d)))))\n496\t                      (throw e)))))]\n497\t    (when (not= id root)\n498\t      (throw (ex-info \"noncanonical\" {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/kind :noncanonical-cursor-cells\n499\t                                      :yin.k/path [root]})))\n500\t    task))\n501\t\n502\t(defn error [f]\n503\t  (try (f) nil (catch Throwable e (or (ex-data e) {:throwable (str e)}))))\n504\t\n505\t(defn do-root\n506\t  \"Root id, {:refused ...} for the tie refusal, or {:resource-limit path}.\"\n507\t  [task]\n508\t  (try (:yin.k/root (emit* task))\n509\t       (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n510\t         (let [d (ex-data e)]\n511\t           (case (:yin.k/kind d)\n512\t             :unresolved-cursor-cells {:refused d}\n513\t             :resource-limit {:resource-limit (:yin.k/path d)}\n514\t             (throw e))))))\n515\t\n516\t(defn safe-6a-root [task]\n517\t  (try (:yin.k/root (rows/emit task))\n518\t       (catch Throwable e {:refused (select-keys (ex-data e) [:yin.k/kind :yin.k/path])})))\n519\t\n520\t;; ------------------------------------------------------------ generators\n521\t\n522\t(defn rename-and-shuffle\n523\t  \"Rename every cursor cell by `renaming` and shuffle every :set, :map and\n524\t   the census in listed order (shuffle is rebound by callers).\"\n525\t  [n renaming]\n526\t  (letfn [(value [v] (case (first v)\n527\t                       :cursor-cell [:cursor-cell (bij (second v))]\n528\t                       :row [:row (go (second v))]\n529\t                       v))\n530\t          (bij [x] (get renaming x x))\n531\t          (go [n]\n532\t            (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n]\n533\t              (case kind\n534\t                :set (rows/node :set (vec (shuffle (mapv value slots))))\n535\t                :map (rows/node :map (vec (mapcat identity (shuffle (mapv (fn [[k v]] [(value k) (value v)]) (partition 2 slots))))))\n536\t                :cursor-cells (rows/node :cursor-cells (vec (mapcat (fn [[c b]] [(bij c) (go b)]) (shuffle (mapv vec (partition 2 slots))))))\n537\t                (rows/node kind (mapv (fn [d x]\n538\t                                        (cond (ref? d) (go x)\n539\t                                              (refs? d) (mapv go x)\n540\t                                              (= :C d) (bij x)\n541\t                                              (v? d) (if x (value x) x)\n542\t                                              :else x))\n543\t                                      (descriptors kind slots) slots)))))]\n544\t    (go n)))\n545\t\n546\t(defn reorder\n547\t  \"The task with f applied to the listed members of every :set and :map, in\n548\t   walk order (f gets the container's ordinal and its members, a map's as\n549\t   [k v] pairs); install children included; census untouched.\"\n550\t  [task f]\n551\t  (let [i (atom -1)]\n552\t    (letfn [(value [v] (case (first v) :row [:row (go (second v))] v))\n553\t            (go [n]\n554\t              (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n]\n555\t                (case kind\n556\t                  :set (let [k (swap! i inc) ms (mapv value slots)] (rows/node :set (vec (f k ms))))\n557\t                  :map (let [k (swap! i inc) ps (mapv (fn [[a b]] [(value a) (value b)]) (partition 2 slots))]\n558\t                         (rows/node :map (vec (mapcat identity (f k ps)))))\n559\t                  (rows/node kind (mapv (fn [d x]\n560\t                                          (cond (ref? d) (go x)\n561\t                                                (refs? d) (mapv go x)\n562\t                                                (v? d) (if x (value x) x)\n563\t                                                :else x))\n564\t                                        (descriptors kind slots) slots)))))]\n565\t      (go task))))\n566\t\n567\t(defn all-census-cells\n568\t  \"Source ids of every census in the tree (root and install children).\"\n569\t  [task]\n570\t  (let [acc (atom [])]\n571\t    (letfn [(node [n] (when (map? n)\n572\t                        (when (= :cursor-cells (:kind n)) (swap! acc into (take-nth 2 (:slots n))))\n573\t                        (doseq [[d x] (map vector (descriptors (:kind n) (:slots n)) (:slots n))]\n574\t                          (cond (ref? d) (node x) (refs? d) (run! node x)\n575\t                                (v? d) (when (and x (= :row (first x))) (node (second x)))))))]\n576\t      (node task) (vec @acc))))\n577\t\n578\t(defn seeded-shuffle [^java.util.Random r]\n579\t  (fn [xs] (let [a (java.util.ArrayList. ^java.util.Collection (vec xs))]\n580\t             (java.util.Collections/shuffle a r)\n581\t             (vec a))))\n582\t\n583\t(defn decoded\n584\t  \"Portable decoded equality of an abstract value (check-abstract!'s rule).\"\n585\t  [v]\n586\t  (case (first v)\n587\t    :lit [:lit (second v)]\n588\t    :cursor-cell [:identity (second v)]\n589\t    :row (let [n (second v) ss (:slots n)]\n590\t           (case (:kind n)\n591\t             :vec [:seq (mapv decoded ss)]\n592\t             :set [:set (set (map decoded ss))]\n593\t             :map [:map (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [(decoded k) (decoded x)])) (partition 2 ss))]\n594\t             [:row n]))))\n595\t\n596\t(defn distinct-decoded [vs]\n597\t  (vec (vals (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (pr-str %1) (pr-str %2))) (map (fn [e] [(decoded e) e])) vs))))\n598\t\n599\t(defn gen-value\n600\t  \"Random V over `cells`, depth-bounded: literals, cursor cells, vectors,\n601\t   sets, maps (cursor cells as keys too), sets of cursor-cell pairs (edges,\n602\t   aliases such as [X X] included), sets of sets.\"\n603\t  [^java.util.Random r cells depth]\n604\t  (let [pick (fn [xs] (nth xs (.nextInt r (count xs))))\n605\t        cc (fn [] [:cursor-cell (pick cells)])\n606\t        k (.nextInt r (if (pos? depth) 9 3))]\n607\t    (case k\n608\t      0 [:lit (pick [1 2 :k \"s\" nil])]\n609\t      1 (cc)\n610\t      2 (cc)\n611\t      3 (let [elems (vec (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 3)) #(gen-value r cells (dec depth))))]\n612\t          (if (some #(not= :lit (first %)) elems) [:row (rows/node :vec elems)] [:lit (mapv second elems)]))\n613\t      4 (let [elems (distinct-decoded (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 4)) #(gen-value r cells (dec depth))))]\n614\t          (if (some #(not= :lit (first %)) elems) [:row (rows/node :set elems)] [:lit (set (map second elems))]))\n615\t      5 (let [pairs (vec (vals (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (pr-str %1) (pr-str %2))) (map (fn [p] [(decoded (first p)) p]))\n616\t                                     (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 3)) #(vector (gen-value r cells (dec depth)) (gen-value r cells (dec depth)))))))]\n617\t          (if (some (fn [[a b]] (or (not= :lit (first a)) (not= :lit (first b)))) pairs)\n618\t            [:row (rows/node :map (vec (mapcat identity pairs)))]\n619\t            [:lit (into {} (map (fn [[a b]] [(second a) (second b)])) pairs)]))\n620\t      (6 7) (let [edges (distinct-decoded (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt r 3)) #(vector :row (rows/node :vec [(cc) (cc)]))))]\n621\t              [:row (rows/node :set edges)])\n622\t      8 (let [inner (distinct-decoded (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt r 2))\n623\t                                                  #(let [es (distinct-decoded (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 3)) cc))]\n624\t                                                     [:row (rows/node :set es)])))]\n625\t          [:row (rows/node :set inner)]))))\n626\t\n627\t(defn reached [v]\n628\t  (let [acc (atom #{})]\n629\t    (letfn [(w [v] (case (first v)\n630\t                     :cursor-cell (swap! acc conj (second v))\n631\t                     :row (doseq [s (:slots (second v))] (w s))\n632\t                     nil))]\n633\t      (w v) @acc)))\n634\t\n635\t(defn gen-task\n636\t  \"A :halted task: 1-6 cursor cells over two bodies (ties common), 1-3 store\n637\t   bindings and the result slot hold random values.\"\n638\t  [seed]\n639\t  (let [r (java.util.Random. seed)\n640\t        k (inc (.nextInt r 6))\n641\t        cells (mapv #(keyword \"src\" (str \"c\" %)) (range k))\n642\t        bodies (mapv (fn [_] (rt/cursor-cell-body :s (if (zero? (.nextInt r 3)) 1 0))) cells)\n643\t        names (vec (take (inc (.nextInt r 3)) '[a b c]))\n644\t        vals (mapv (fn [_] (gen-value r cells 3)) names)\n645\t        result (gen-value r cells 2)\n646\t        used (reduce into (reached result) (map reached vals))\n647\t        census (keep (fn [[c b]] (when (used c) [c b])) (map vector cells bodies))]\n648\t    (if (empty? used)\n649\t      (recur (inc seed))\n650\t      (let [t (rt/task-node census result)]\n651\t        (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots t) 6 (rows/node :store (vec (mapcat (fn [n v] [n v]) names vals)))))))))\n652\t\n653\t(defn gen-incidence-task\n654\t  \"The reviewer's tie-heavy incidence families (r3 review, seed-driven):\n655\t   2-8 cells of one body; edge sets, overlapping groups, aliased maps,\n656\t   repeated and nested containers, reversed edges, ordered anchors.\"\n657\t  [seed]\n658\t  (let [r (java.util.Random. seed)\n659\t        sh (seeded-shuffle r)\n660\t        c (fn [x] [:cursor-cell x])\n661\t        v (fn [xs] [:row (rows/node :vec (vec xs))])\n662\t        s (fn [xs] [:row (rows/node :set (distinct-decoded xs))])\n663\t        m (fn [ps] [:row (rows/node :map (vec (mapcat identity (vals (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (pr-str %1) (pr-str %2)))\n664\t                                                                             (map (fn [p] [(decoded (first p)) p])) ps)))))])\n665\t        n (+ 2 (.nextInt r 7)) cs (mapv #(keyword \"src\" (str \"i\" %)) (range n))\n666\t        cc #(c (nth cs (.nextInt r n)))\n667\t        edge #(v [(cc) (cc)]) es (vec (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt r 9)) edge))\n668\t        group #(s (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt r 4)) cc))\n669\t        value (case (mod seed 10)\n670\t                0 (s es)\n671\t                1 (v [(s es) (s (sh es))])\n672\t                2 (s (repeatedly 4 group))\n673\t                3 (v [(s es) (cc)])\n674\t                4 (s (map #(v [% (group)]) es))\n675\t                5 (m (mapv (fn [x] [(c x) (cc)]) cs))\n676\t                6 (v [(s es) (s (map #(v (reverse (:slots (second %)))) es))])\n677\t                7 (s (map #(m [[(cc) %] [[:lit :anchor] (group)]]) es))\n678\t                8 (s [(v [(s es) (group)]) (v [(group) (s (sh es))])])\n679\t                9 (v [(s es) (s (repeatedly 4 group)) (cc)]))\n680\t        b (rt/cursor-cell-body :s 0)]\n681\t    (rt/task-node (mapv #(vector % b) (sort (reached value))) value)))\n682\t\n683\t(defn worked-act []\n684\t  (first (:slots (rows/decode (rows/frame->rows ft/worked-frame)))))\n685\t\n686\t(def park-vector [[:closure 0 [] 2] [:halt 0] [:park 0] [:return 0]])\n687\t(def park-address (jing/segment-key park-vector))\n688\t\n689\t(defn frame-task\n690\t  \"A blocked task carrying the worked code plus a park segment. The wait's\n691\t   act holds `wait-values` in its window register 1 and in one K frame's\n692\t   window register 1; `env-value`, when given, is bound to e0 in the free\n693\t   environment and in every environment; the parked state (P 7) is an act\n694\t   at the park site whose K frame holds `parked-value` in register 1.\n695\t   Decodes under 6a's validate-frames.\"\n696\t  [census wait-values env-value parked-value]\n697\t  (let [base (rt/task-node (conj (vec census) [:test/cursor (rt/cursor-cell-body :s 0)]) nil)\n698\t        [seg pc env window k rd] (:slots (worked-act))\n699\t        [_ store-of] (:slots env)\n700\t        bindings (rows/node :bindings (if env-value ['e0 env-value] []))\n701\t        env (rows/node :env [bindings store-of])\n702\t        kframe (fn [v] (rows/node :kframe [seg pc env (rows/node :window [1 v]) rd]))\n703\t        [w1 w2] wait-values\n704\t        wait-act (rows/node :act [seg pc env (rows/node :window [1 w1]) (rows/node :k (if w2 [(kframe w2)] [])) rd])\n705\t        pending (second (:slots (rows/decode (rows/frame->rows ft/worked-frame))))\n706\t        parked (rows/node :act [park-address 3 env (rows/node :window []) (rows/node :k [(kframe parked-value)]) 0])]\n707\t    (rows/node :task (-> (:slots base) (assoc 2 :blocked) (assoc 5 bindings)\n708\t                         (assoc 11 (merge ft/worked-code {park-address park-vector}))\n709\t                         (assoc 8 (rows/node :parked-table (if parked-value [7 parked] [])))\n710\t                         (assoc 13 [(rows/node :wait [wait-act pending])]) (assoc 16 {:yin.k/policy :yin.k/fork})))))\n711\t\n712\t(defn gen-frame-task [seed]\n713\t  (let [r (java.util.Random. seed)\n714\t        k (inc (.nextInt r 4))\n715\t        cells (mapv #(keyword \"src\" (str \"f\" %)) (range k))\n716\t        body (rt/cursor-cell-body :s 0)\n717\t        pick (fn [] (gen-value r cells 2))\n718\t        wait-values (vec (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 2)) pick))\n719\t        env-value (when (zero? (.nextInt r 2)) (pick))\n720\t        parked-value (when (zero? (.nextInt r 2)) (pick))\n721\t        used (reduce into #{} (map reached (remove nil? (concat wait-values [env-value parked-value]))))]\n722\t    (if (empty? used)\n723\t      (recur (inc seed))\n724\t      (frame-task (mapv #(vector % body) (filter used cells)) wait-values env-value parked-value))))\n725\t\n726\t(defn gen-child-task\n727\t  \"A parent (seed) with two install children: one random child task and the\n728\t   review counterexample as a child; the parent's own values stay random.\"\n729\t  [seed]\n730\t  (let [parent (gen-task seed)\n731\t        child (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots (gen-task (+ 100000 seed))) 3 :child))]\n732\t    (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots parent) 12 [(rows/node :install ['a :running nil {} child])\n733\t                                                (rows/node :install ['b :running nil {} child])]))))\n734\t\n735\t(defn fixture-review-counterexample\n736\t  \"'a bound to #{X Y} with equal bodies, 'b bound to X.\"\n737\t  []\n738\t  (let [body (rt/cursor-cell-body :s 0)\n739\t        t (rt/task-node [[:x body] [:y body]] [:lit nil])]\n740\t    (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots t) 6 (rows/node :store ['a [:row (rows/node :set [[:cursor-cell :x] [:cursor-cell :y]])]\n741\t                                                             'b [:cursor-cell :x]])))))\n742\t\n743\t(defn with-child\n744\t  \"`parent` with one install 'a holding `child` (slot 3 set to :child).\"\n745\t  [parent child]\n746\t  (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots parent) 12\n747\t                          [(rows/node :install ['a :running nil {} (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots child) 3 :child))])])))\n748\t\n749\t;; ------------------------------------------------------------ diagnostics\n750\t\n751\t(defn- permutations [n]\n752\t  (if (zero? n) [[]]\n753\t      (for [p (permutations (dec n)) i (range n)]\n754\t        (vec (concat (subvec p 0 i) [(dec n)] (subvec p i))))))\n755\t\n756\t(defn- factorial [n] (reduce * 1 (range 1 (inc n))))\n757\t\n758\t(defn- container-sizes\n759\t  \"Member count of every :set and :map, indexed by the ordinal reorder gives it.\"\n760\t  [task]\n761\t  (let [acc (atom {})]\n762\t    (reorder task (fn [k ms] (swap! acc assoc k (count ms)) ms))\n763\t    (mapv @acc (range (count @acc)))))\n764\t\n765\t(defn- permissive-root [t]\n766\t  (binding [*numbering-opts* (assoc *numbering-opts* :permissive true)]\n767\t    (let [d (discovery-numbering t)] (first (emit-node* t (:numbering d) {} [])))))\n768\t\n769\t(defn classify-refused\n770\t  \"For a refused state: :interchangeable when every listed order of every\n771\t   set and map gives one root under permissive entry (exhaustive when the\n772\t   number of orders is at most `limit`), :non-interchangeable when two\n773\t   orders differ (exhaustive or sampled), else :undecided (sampled, one\n774\t   root). Permissive entry depends on nothing but listed orders, so the\n775\t   exhaustive verdict is exact.\"\n776\t  [task limit samples]\n777\t  (let [sizes (container-sizes task)\n778\t        total (reduce (fn [t n] (min (* t (factorial n)) 1000000000)) 1 sizes)]\n779\t    (if (<= total limit)\n780\t      (let [choices (reduce (fn [acc n] (for [c acc p (permutations n)] (conj c p))) [[]] sizes)\n781\t            roots (into #{} (map (fn [perms] (permissive-root (reorder task (fn [k ms] (mapv #(nth ms %) (nth perms k))))))) choices)]\n782\t        (if (= 1 (count roots)) :interchangeable :non-interchangeable))\n783\t      (let [r (java.util.Random. 7) sh (seeded-shuffle r)\n784\t            roots (into #{} (map (fn [_] (permissive-root (reorder task (fn [_ ms] (sh ms)))))) (range samples))]\n785\t        (if (= 1 (count roots)) :undecided :non-interchangeable)))))\n786\t\n787\t(defn invariant-roots\n788\t  \"Distinct roots of a state over `n` renamings plus shuffles (1 = invariant\n789\t   under the samples).\"\n790\t  [task n]\n791\t  (let [r (java.util.Random. 5) cells (all-census-cells task)]\n792\t    (with-redefs [shuffle (seeded-shuffle r)]\n793\t      (->> (repeatedly n #(rename-and-shuffle task (zipmap cells (map (fn [i] (keyword \"r\" (str \"z\" i))) (shuffle (range (count cells)))))))\n794\t           ;; A refusal's :cursor-cells names local source ids; the verdict and\n795\t           ;; the path are what must be invariant.\n796\t           (map (fn [t] (let [r (do-root t)] (if (map? r) (update r :refused dissoc :yin.k/cursor-cells) r))))\n797\t           distinct count))))\n798\t\n799\t(defn report-fixture [name task]\n800\t  (let [d (discovery-numbering task)]\n801\t    (println name)\n802\t    (println \"  DO :\" (or (:refused d) (into (sorted-map) (:numbering d))) \"| work\" (:work (:used d)) \"| encoded bytes\" (:encoded-bytes (:used d)))\n803\t    (println \"  DO root:\" (do-root task) \"| roots over 24 renamings+shuffles:\" (invariant-roots task 24))\n804\t    (when (:refused d) (println \"  interchangeable? (exhaustive/sampled permissive):\" (classify-refused task 5040 48)))\n805\t    (println \"  6a root:\" (safe-6a-root task))))\n806\t\n807\t(defn invariance-check\n808\t  \"Root of the state and of the state renamed and shuffled; decode of the\n809\t   carrier. Returns a map of outcomes.\"\n810\t  [task ^java.util.Random r]\n811\t  (let [cells (all-census-cells task)\n812\t        fresh (zipmap cells (map #(keyword \"other\" (str \"z\" %)) (shuffle (range (count cells)))))\n813\t        task2 (with-redefs [shuffle (seeded-shuffle r)] (rename-and-shuffle task fresh))\n814\t        d1 (do-root task) d2 (do-root task2)]\n815\t    (cond\n816\t      (and (map? d1) (:refused d1))\n817\t      {:refused (:refused d1) :invariant (= (dissoc (:refused d1) :yin.k/cursor-cells) (dissoc (:refused d2) :yin.k/cursor-cells))}\n818\t      (map? d1) {:resource-limit (:resource-limit d1)}\n819\t      :else\n820\t      {:root d1 :invariant (= d1 d2)\n821\t       :used (:used (discovery-numbering task))\n822\t       :decode (let [e (error #(decode* (emit* task)))]\n823\t                 (cond (nil? e) :ok\n824\t                       (= :resource-limit (:yin.k/kind e)) :sixa-recompute-limit\n825\t                       :else e))})))\n826\t\n827\t(defn search [label gen seeds]\n828\t  (let [r (java.util.Random. 11)\n829\t        stats (atom {:numbered 0 :refused 0 :resource-limit 0 :invariance-fail 0\n830\t                     :decode-ok 0 :decode-fail 0 :decode-6a-limit 0\n831\t                     :refused-interchangeable 0 :refused-non-interchangeable 0 :refused-undecided 0\n832\t                     :refused-only-across-groups 0 :refused-reasons {}\n833\t                     :count-spelling-gain 0 :count-spelling-loss 0\n834\t                     :max-work 0 :max-encoded-bytes 0 :max-local-runs 0})]\n835\t    (doseq [seed seeds]\n836\t      (let [task (gen seed) o (invariance-check task r)\n837\t            without (binding [*numbering-opts* (assoc *numbering-opts* :count-spelling false)] (do-root task))]\n838\t        ;; The occurrence count in the key: states it numbers that the literal\n839\t        ;; direction (body rank and local index only) refuses, and the reverse.\n840\t        (when (and (:root o) (map? without) (:refused without)) (swap! stats update :count-spelling-gain inc))\n841\t        (when (and (:refused o) (keyword? without)) (swap! stats update :count-spelling-loss inc))\n842\t        (when-not (:invariant o true)\n843\t          (swap! stats update :invariance-fail inc) (println \"INVARIANCE FAIL\" label seed))\n844\t        (cond\n845\t          (:refused o)\n846\t          (let [why (:probe/why (:refused o))]\n847\t            (swap! stats update :refused inc)\n848\t            (doseq [w why] (swap! stats update-in [:refused-reasons w] (fnil inc 0)))\n849\t            (when (every? #{:shared-across-groups} why) (swap! stats update :refused-only-across-groups inc))\n850\t            (swap! stats update (case (classify-refused task 720 48)\n851\t                                  :interchangeable :refused-interchangeable\n852\t                                  :non-interchangeable :refused-non-interchangeable\n853\t                                  :refused-undecided) inc))\n854\t          (:resource-limit o)\n855\t          (do (swap! stats update :resource-limit inc) (println \"RESOURCE LIMIT\" label seed (:resource-limit o)))\n856\t          :else\n857\t          (do (swap! stats update :numbered inc)\n858\t              (swap! stats update :max-work max (:work (:used o) 0))\n859\t              (swap! stats update :max-encoded-bytes max (:encoded-bytes (:used o) 0))\n860\t              (swap! stats update :max-local-runs max (:local-runs (:used o) 0))\n861\t              (case (:decode o)\n862\t                :ok (swap! stats update :decode-ok inc)\n863\t                :sixa-recompute-limit (swap! stats update :decode-6a-limit inc)\n864\t                (do (swap! stats update :decode-fail inc) (println \"DECODE FAIL\" label seed (:decode o))))))))\n865\t    (println label (count seeds) \"states:\" @stats)\n866\t    @stats))\n867\t\n868\t(defn -main []\n869\t  (let [body (rt/cursor-cell-body :s 0)\n870\t        body1 (rt/cursor-cell-body :s 1)\n871\t        s (fn [es] [:row (rows/node :set es)])\n872\t        v (fn [cs] [:row (rows/node :vec (mapv #(vector :cursor-cell %) cs))])\n873\t        c (fn [x] [:cursor-cell x])\n874\t        task (fn [ids result] (rt/task-node (mapv #(vector % body) ids) result))\n875\t        two-cycle (task [:a :b] (s [(v [:a :b]) (v [:b :a])]))\n876\t        three-cycle (task [:a :b :c] (s [(v [:a :b]) (v [:b :c]) (v [:c :a])]))\n877\t        path-abc (task [:a :b :c] (s [(v [:a :b]) (v [:b :c])]))\n878\t        loop-2cycle (task [:l :a :b] (s [(v [:l :l]) (v [:a :b]) (v [:b :a])]))\n879\t        seven (rt/seven-cursor-cell-triangle-square)\n880\t        witness (task [:a :b] [:row (rows/node :vec [(s [(s [(v [:a :b]) (v [:b :a])])]) (c :a)])])\n881\t        mixed (rt/task-node [[:a body] [:b body1] [:c body1]] (s [(v [:a :b]) (v [:a :c])]))\n882\t        anchored (task [:a :b :c :d :e] [:row (rows/node :vec [(s [(v [:a :b]) (v [:a :c]) (v [:b :d]) (v [:c :e]) (v [:d :b]) (v [:e :c])]) (c :a)])])\n883\t        two-sets-shared (task [:x :y :z] [:row (rows/node :vec [(s [(c :x) (c :y)]) (s [(c :y) (c :z)])])])\n884\t        two-sets-equal (task [:x :y] [:row (rows/node :vec [(s [(c :x) (c :y)]) (s [(c :x) (c :y)])])])\n885\t        two-2cycles (task [:a :b :c :d] (s [(s [(v [:a :b]) (v [:b :a])]) (s [(v [:c :d]) (v [:d :c])])]))\n886\t        nested-vs-edges (task [:x :y :z :w] [:row (rows/node :vec [(s [(s [(c :x) (c :y)])]) (s [(v [:x :z]) (v [:y :w])])])])]\n887\t    (println \"== fixtures (base design)\")\n888\t    (report-fixture \"fixture :s1 :s2 :x :y (6a pin fab223...)\" (rt/fixture :s1 :s2 :x :y))\n889\t    (report-fixture \"review counterexample 'a #{X Y}, 'b X\" (fixture-review-counterexample))\n890\t    (report-fixture \"symmetric pair #{X Y}\" (task [:x :y] (s [(c :x) (c :y)])))\n891\t    (report-fixture \"alias a: [x x y]\" (task [:x :y] (v [:x :x :y])))\n892\t    (report-fixture \"alias b: [x y y]\" (task [:x :y] (v [:x :y :y])))\n893\t    (report-fixture \"#{[X X] [Y Y]}\" (task [:x :y] (s [(v [:x :x]) (v [:y :y])])))\n894\t    (report-fixture \"{X 1, Y 1}\" (task [:x :y] [:row (rows/node :map [(c :x) [:lit 1] (c :y) [:lit 1]])]))\n895\t    (report-fixture \"codex A: #{[X X] [Y Z]}\" (task [:x :y :z] (s [(v [:x :x]) (v [:y :z])])))\n896\t    (report-fixture \"codex A reversed\" (task [:x :y :z] (s [(v [:y :z]) (v [:x :x])])))\n897\t    (report-fixture \"codex B: {X X, Y Z}\" (task [:x :y :z] [:row (rows/node :map [(c :x) (c :x) (c :y) (c :z)])]))\n898\t    (report-fixture \"codex C: #{#{X Y} #{Z W}}\" (task [:x :y :z :w] (s [(s [(c :x) (c :y)]) (s [(c :z) (c :w)])])))\n899\t    (report-fixture \"codex C renamed\" (task [:q :r :s :t] (s [(s [(c :s) (c :t)]) (s [(c :q) (c :r)])])))\n900\t    (report-fixture \"[#{X Y} X]\" (task [:x :y] [:row (rows/node :vec [(s [(c :x) (c :y)]) (c :x)])]))\n901\t    (report-fixture \"[#{#{X Y} #{Z W}} X]\" (task [:x :y :z :w] [:row (rows/node :vec [(s [(s [(c :x) (c :y)]) (s [(c :z) (c :w)])]) (c :x)])]))\n902\t    (report-fixture \"#{[#{X Y} #{X Y}] [#{P Q} #{R S}]}\"\n903\t                    (task [:x :y :p :q :r :s] (s [[:row (rows/node :vec [(s [(c :x) (c :y)]) (s [(c :x) (c :y)])])]\n904\t                                                   [:row (rows/node :vec [(s [(c :p) (c :q)]) (s [(c :r) (c :s)])])]])))\n905\t    (report-fixture \"codex r2 witness [#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]\" witness)\n906\t    (report-fixture \"[#{X Y} #{Y Z}] (occurrence count separates Y)\" two-sets-shared)\n907\t    (report-fixture \"path #{[A B] [B C]} (occurrence count separates B)\" path-abc)\n908\t    (report-fixture \"ten cells in a vec\" (let [ids (mapv #(keyword \"src\" (str \"x\" %)) (range 10))]\n909\t                                           (rt/task-node (mapv (fn [id i] [id (rt/cursor-cell-body :s i)]) ids (range)) (v ids))))\n910\t    (println \"\\n== refused fixtures (tie test fails), with the exact interchangeability verdict\")\n911\t    (report-fixture \"2-cycle #{[A B] [B A]}\" two-cycle)\n912\t    (report-fixture \"3-cycle #{[A B] [B C] [C A]}\" three-cycle)\n913\t    (report-fixture \"loop + 2-cycle #{[L L] [A B] [B A]} (6a pinned 55ff16...)\" loop-2cycle)\n914\t    (report-fixture \"seven-cell triangle+square\" seven)\n915\t    (report-fixture \"[#{X Y} #{X Y}] (shared across groups)\" two-sets-equal)\n916\t    (report-fixture \"codex r3 ex.1 mixed bodies #{[A B] [A C]}, A body 0, B C body 1\" mixed)\n917\t    (report-fixture \"codex r3 ex.2 anchored [#{[A B] [A C] [B D] [C E] [D B] [E C]} A]\" anchored)\n918\t    (report-fixture \"#{#{[A B] [B A]} #{[C D] [D C]}} (incomplete keys)\" two-2cycles)\n919\t    (report-fixture \"[#{#{X Y}} #{[X Z] [Y W]}] (key walk accepts inside, root refuses)\" nested-vs-edges)\n920\t    (println \"\\n== install child refusal translates in decode (path prefixed by the root id, then [12 name ...])\")\n921\t    (let [parent (with-child (rt/task-node [] [:lit nil]) two-cycle)]\n922\t      (println \"  lift:\" (error #(emit* parent)))\n923\t      (println \"  decode of a carrier built with emit-numbered:\" (error #(decode* (rows/emit-numbered parent {})))))\n924\t    (println \"\\n== gates and budgets (resource refusals, never canonicality verdicts)\")\n925\t    (binding [*numbering-opts* {:budget {:work 1}}]\n926\t      (println \"  loop+2-cycle {:work 1}:\" (error #(emit* loop-2cycle)))\n927\t      (println \"  decode of a valid carrier under {:work 1}:\" (error #(decode* (binding [*numbering-opts* {}] (emit* (rt/fixture :s1 :s2 :x :y)))))))\n928\t    (binding [*numbering-opts* {:budget {:cursor-cells 1}}]\n929\t      (println \"  two cells under {:cursor-cells 1}:\" (error #(emit* (task [:x :y] (v [:x :y]))))))\n930\t    (binding [*numbering-opts* {:budget {:depth 3}}]\n931\t      (println \"  [[[[X]]]] under {:depth 3}:\" (error #(emit* (task [:x] [:row (rows/node :vec [[:row (rows/node :vec [[:row (rows/node :vec [(c :x)])]])]])])))))\n932\t    (let [ids (mapv #(keyword \"src\" (str \"n\" %)) (range 65))]\n933\t      (println \"  65 cells under the default budget:\" (error #(emit* (rt/task-node (mapv (fn [id i] [id (rt/cursor-cell-body :s i)]) ids (range)) (v ids))))))\n934\t    (println \"\\n== large literals: never spelled in an ordered position; charged before encoding in an unordered one\")\n935\t    (let [large (vec (range 400000))\n936\t          reachable (task [:x] [:row (rows/node :vec [(c :x) [:lit large]])])\n937\t          in-set (task [:x :y] (s [[:row (rows/node :vec [(c :x) [:lit large]])] [:row (rows/node :vec [(c :y) [:lit large]])]]))\n938\t          unreachable (rt/task-node [[:x body]] [:lit large])]\n939\t      (println \"  ordered: root\" (do-root reachable) \"| work\" (:work (:used (discovery-numbering reachable))))\n940\t      (println \"  unordered:\" (do-root in-set))\n941\t      (println \"  unreachable census cell (totality defect, not a refusal):\" (error #(discovery-numbering unreachable))))\n942\t    (println \"\\n== key bytes versus stream descriptor size (rank spelling)\")\n943\t    (doseq [n [128 65536]]\n944\t      (let [big (fn [i] (rows/node :cursor-cell-body [(rows/node :stream [:s (apply str (repeat n \"d\"))]) i]))\n945\t            t (rt/task-node [[:x (big 0)] [:y (big 0)] [:z (big 1)] [:w (big 1)]]\n946\t                            (s [(s [(c :x) (c :y)]) (s [(c :z) (c :w)]) (s [(c :x) (c :z)])]))\n947\t            d (discovery-numbering t)]\n948\t        (println \"  descriptor\" n \"chars: work\" (:work (:used d)) \"| encoded bytes\" (:encoded-bytes (:used d))\n949\t                 \"| local runs\" (:local-runs (:used d)) \"| root\" (do-root t))))\n950\t    (println \"\\n== frame-bearing fixtures (act window, K frame window, environments, parked state)\")\n951\t    (let [t (frame-task [[:x body] [:y body]] [(c :x) (c :y)] (c :y) (s [(c :x) (c :y)]))]\n952\t      (report-fixture \"wait window x, K window y, env y, parked K window #{x y}\" t)\n953\t      (println \"  decode:\" (or (error #(decode* (emit* t))) :ok)))\n954\t    (let [t (frame-task [[:x body] [:y body]] [(s [(c :x) (c :y)])] nil (c :y))]\n955\t      (report-fixture \"wait window #{x y}, parked K window y\" t)\n956\t      (println \"  decode:\" (or (error #(decode* (emit* t))) :ok)))\n957\t    (println \"\\n== install children numbered by discovery order\")\n958\t    (let [child (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots (fixture-review-counterexample)) 3 :child))\n959\t          parent (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots (rt/task-node [[:x (rt/cursor-cell-body :root/s 1)]] (c :x))) 12\n960\t                                         [(rows/node :install ['a :running nil {} child])\n961\t                                          (rows/node :install ['b :running nil {} child])]))\n962\t          wire (emit* parent)]\n963\t      (println \"  parent root:\" (:yin.k/root wire) \"| task rows:\" (count (filter #(= :task (second %)) (:yin.k/rows wire)))\n964\t               \"| child numbering:\" (into (sorted-map) (:numbering (discovery-numbering child)))\n965\t               \"| decode:\" (or (error #(decode* wire)) :ok)))\n966\t    (println \"\\n== random search (refused states classified by exhaustive permissive entry when <= 720 orders, else 48 samples)\")\n967\t    (search \"random values\" gen-task (range 2000))\n968\t    (search \"frame-bearing\" gen-frame-task (range 200))\n969\t    (search \"with children\" gen-child-task (range 100))\n970\t    (search \"incidence families (reviewer's generator)\" gen-incidence-task (range 1000))))\n971\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"704437a3-7e24-494b-ab26-b13fa72d3d40","uuid":"3243634b-8327-4f4b-8690-9635e0e3e1ec","timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:43:16.019Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-numbering/collab/numbering-probe/src/probe/discovery.clj","content":"(ns probe.discovery\n  \"Prototype of discovery-order cursor-cell numbering, the BASE design of the\n   note of 2026-10-12 (round 4), over the 6a abstract task representation\n   (yin.vm.ucf.rows). Not repo code; a scratch project under collab/. The\n   round-3 variants (components, residue search) live in probe.discovery-r3.\n\n   Vocabulary: UCF 7.5.3. A cursor cell is the VM box the carrier serializes;\n   its source id is the lift's local name; the procedure assigns :yin.k/cc-n.\n\n   The rule. A cursor cell gets the next number the first time the walk meets\n   it. The walk is pre-order over the task in table order. A guest :set or\n   :map is turned into a vector of its members (a map entry as [:entry k v])\n   sorted by KEY: the spelling of a local walk over the member under the\n   current numbering, with numbered cells spelled by number and unnumbered\n   ones by local first-occurrence index, body rank and occurrence count.\n   Members whose keys tie are POSTPONED to the run's queue and re-keyed after\n   the rest of the walk, until a pass numbers nothing. A remaining tie group\n   is entered in listed order when the TIE TEST holds (common key complete;\n   the members' unnumbered cells pairwise disjoint and occurring in no member\n   of another remaining group); otherwise the root walk refuses\n   :yin.k/non-portable :unresolved-cursor-cells and a key walk spells the\n   group as [:tie K ... K] in its key.\n\n   Budgets: :cursor-cells (census size, first), :depth (nesting of the walk),\n   :work (one unit per position visited or spelled, plus 6a's representation\n   bound of every value before it is CBOR-encoded for a comparison). Exceeding\n   one is :yin.k/unsupported :resource-limit, never a canonicality verdict.\n\n   Diagnostic switches (*numbering-opts*): :permissive enters a failing group\n   in listed order instead of refusing (used to test interchangeability by\n   exhaustion or sampling); :count-spelling false drops the occurrence count\n   from the key (the owner's literal direction, for measurement).\"\n  (:require [clojure.set :as set]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-test :as rt]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]))\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- schema\n\n(def synthetic-table\n  \"The one row that exists only inside the procedure: a :map entry as an\n   ordered pair, so the alias pattern across key and value is in its key.\"\n  {:entry [:V :V]})\n\n(defn descriptors [kind slots]\n  (let [schema (or (get rows/row-table kind) (get synthetic-table kind))]\n    (cond (= schema :pending) (into [:D] (get rows/pending-table (first slots)))\n          (= :repeat (first schema)) (vec (repeat (count slots) (second schema)))\n          (= :pairs (first schema)) (vec (take (count slots) (cycle (rest schema))))\n          :else schema)))\n\n(defn ref? [d] (and (vector? d) (= :ref (first d))))\n(defn refs? [d] (and (vector? d) (= :refs (first d))))\n(defn v? [d] (contains? #{:V :optional-V} d))\n\n(defn bytes-key\n  \"Uncharged encoding; generators and diagnostics only.\"\n  [x] (mapv #(bit-and (int %) 255) (seq (cbor/encode x))))\n\n(defn compare-bytes [a b]\n  (loop [i 0]\n    (cond (= i (count a)) (if (= i (count b)) 0 -1)\n          (= i (count b)) 1\n          (= (nth a i) (nth b i)) (recur (inc i))\n          :else (compare (nth a i) (nth b i)))))\n\n(def keyed-structural #{:bindings :store :parked-table})\n\n(defn elem-item\n  \"The item a member is keyed and entered as: a :set member is its V; a :map\n   entry [k v] is the synthetic ordered row [:entry k v].\"\n  [kind e]\n  (if (= :map kind) [:row {:kind :entry :slots (vec e)}] e))\n\n(defn child-task? [ctx n] (and (= :task (:kind n)) (not (identical? n (:task ctx)))))\n\n;; --------------------------------------------------------------- budgets\n\n(def default-budget\n  \"6a's budget without :label-bytes and :search; :work now also counts\n   representation bytes, so its default takes over :label-bytes' scale.\"\n  (assoc (dissoc rows/default-budget :label-bytes :search) :work 4194304))\n\n(defn- limit! [category]\n  (throw (ex-info \"resource limit\"\n                  {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :resource-limit :yin.k/path [category]})))\n\n(defn- spend! [ctx category amount]\n  (let [n (get (swap! (:counter ctx) update category (fnil + 0) amount) category)]\n    (when (> n (get (:budget ctx) category)) (limit! category))))\n\n(defn- rep-bound\n  \"6a's conservative representation bound (check-label-bytes!): an upper\n   bound of the CBOR bytes of x, computed by reading x and allocating nothing.\"\n  [x]\n  (let [n (cond (cbor/byte-payload? x) (+ 16 (alength ^bytes x))\n                (string? x) (+ 128 (* 4 (count x)))\n                (or (keyword? x) (symbol? x)) (+ 128 (* 4 (count (str x))))\n                (coll? x) (reduce (fn [t v] (+ t (rep-bound v))) 128 (if (map? x) (mapcat identity x) x))\n                :else 128)]\n    (if (meta x) (+ n (rep-bound (meta x))) n)))\n\n(defn- key-bytes!\n  \"Charge the representation bound of x to :work, then encode x for comparison.\n   Every encoding the procedure makes goes through here.\"\n  [ctx x]\n  (spend! ctx :work (rep-bound x))\n  (let [bs (bytes-key x)]\n    (swap! (:counter ctx) update :encoded-bytes (fnil + 0) (count bs))\n    bs))\n\n(defn- sort-by-key!\n  \"xs in the bytewise order of (f x), each encoded once (stable).\"\n  [ctx f xs]\n  (mapv second (sort #(compare-bytes (first %1) (first %2)) (mapv (fn [x] [(key-bytes! ctx (f x)) x]) xs))))\n\n;; ------------------------------------------------------------ cell scans\n\n(defn- walk-cells\n  \"Call f on every cursor cell at a position under slot (d x); census and\n   install children excluded; one :work unit per position.\"\n  [ctx d x f]\n  (letfn [(slot [d x]\n            (spend! ctx :work 1)\n            (cond (ref? d) (node x)\n                  (refs? d) (run! node x)\n                  (= :C d) (f x)\n                  (v? d) (when x (case (first x) :cursor-cell (f (second x)) :row (node (second x)) nil))\n                  :else nil))\n          (node [n]\n            (when-not (or (= :cursor-cells (:kind n)) (child-task? ctx n))\n              (dorun (map slot (descriptors (:kind n) (:slots n)) (:slots n)))))]\n    (slot d x)))\n\n(defn item-cells\n  \"The cursor cells under slot (d x), memoized per procedure on the slot value.\"\n  [ctx d x]\n  (or (get @(:cells-memo ctx) [d x])\n      (let [acc (atom #{})]\n        (walk-cells ctx d x #(swap! acc conj %))\n        (swap! (:cells-memo ctx) assoc [d x] @acc)\n        @acc)))\n\n(defn- occurrence-counts\n  \"Cursor cell -> number of positions of the task holding it.\"\n  [ctx task]\n  (let [acc (atom {})]\n    (walk-cells ctx [:ref :task] task #(swap! acc update % (fnil inc 0)))\n    @acc))\n\n(defn body-label [body]\n  (let [[stream position] (:slots body)]\n    [:body (into [:stream] (:slots stream)) position]))\n\n(defn- body-ranks\n  \"Cursor cell -> rank of its body label among the census's distinct body\n   labels in bytewise order (rank order = label order, so keys stay\n   independent of the descriptor's size).\"\n  [ctx bodies]\n  (let [labels (into {} (map (fn [[c b]] [c (body-label b)])) bodies)\n        ranks (into {} (map-indexed (fn [i l] [l i])) (sort-by-key! ctx identity (distinct (vals labels))))]\n    (into {} (map (fn [[c l]] [c (get ranks l)])) labels)))\n\n;; ------------------------------------------------------------------ runs\n\n(def ^:dynamic *trace* false)\n\n(defn- new-run [ctx num tag next]\n  {:ctx ctx :num (atom num) :tag tag :next (atom next) :groups (atom []) :gid (atom 0) :refused (atom nil)})\n\n(defn- meet!\n  \"W2. A cursor cell met for the first time receives the run's next number.\"\n  [run c]\n  (when-not (contains? @(:num run) c)\n    (let [k @(:next run)]\n      (swap! (:num run) assoc c [(:tag run) k])\n      (swap! (:next run) inc)\n      true)))\n\n(declare enter-node! unordered! local-run spell-slot spell-node)\n\n(defn- enter-slot! [run d x path]\n  (let [ctx (:ctx run)]\n    (spend! ctx :work 1)\n    (when (> (count path) (get (:budget ctx) :depth)) (limit! :depth))\n    (cond (ref? d) (enter-node! run x path)\n          (refs? d) (dorun (map-indexed (fn [i n] (enter-node! run n (conj path i))) x))\n          (= :C d) (meet! run x)\n          (v? d) (when x (case (first x)\n                           :cursor-cell (meet! run (second x))\n                           :row (enter-node! run (second x) path)\n                           nil))\n          :else nil)))\n\n(defn- enter-node!\n  \"W1. Pre-order: table order for slots; ordered repeated slots in order;\n   keyed structural rows in the byte order of the key; :window in register\n   order; installs and module stores by name; :set and :map by keys with\n   ties postponed; census and children not entered.\"\n  [run n path]\n  (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n ctx (:ctx run) ds (descriptors kind slots)]\n    (cond\n      (= :cursor-cells kind) nil\n      (child-task? ctx n) nil\n      (= :task kind)\n      (doseq [[i d x] (map vector (range) ds slots)]\n        (if (contains? #{7 12} i)\n          (doseq [child (sort-by-key! ctx #(first (:slots %)) x)]\n            (enter-node! run child (conj path i (first (:slots child)))))\n          (enter-slot! run d x (conj path i))))\n      (contains? keyed-structural kind)\n      (doseq [[k v] (sort-by-key! ctx first (partition 2 slots))]\n        (enter-slot! run (second ds) v (conj path k)))\n      (= :window kind)\n      (doseq [[r v] (sort-by first (partition 2 slots))] (enter-slot! run :V v (conj path r)))\n      (= :set kind) (unordered! run n :set (vec slots) path)\n      (= :map kind) (unordered! run n :map (mapv vec (partition 2 slots)) path)\n      :else (dorun (map-indexed (fn [i [d x]] (enter-slot! run d x (conj path i))) (map vector ds slots))))))\n\n(defn- unordered!\n  \"The transformation: key every member by a local walk under the numbering\n   at this moment; members with a unique key are entered in key order; a run\n   of equal keys is one tie group, postponed to the run's queue (postponement\n   order: containers in walk order, groups within a container in key order).\n   A member's path is the container's path plus :member (there is no\n   canonical index into an unordered container); a group remembers its\n   container by identity.\"\n  [run container kind elems path]\n  (let [keyed (mapv (fn [e] [(local-run run (elem-item kind e) (conj path :member)) e]) elems)\n        groups (partition-by (comp :bytes first) (sort #(compare-bytes (:bytes (first %1)) (:bytes (first %2))) keyed))]\n    (when (and *trace* (= :n (:tag run)))\n      (println \"  [sort]\" path \"num\" @(:num run))\n      (doseq [g groups] (println \"    \" (if (= 1 (count g)) \"enter\" \"POSTPONE\") (mapv (fn [[r e]] [e (:spell r)]) g))))\n    (doseq [g groups]\n      (if (= 1 (count g))\n        (enter-slot! run :V (elem-item kind (second (first g))) (conj path :member))\n        (swap! (:groups run) conj {:id (swap! (:gid run) inc) :container container :kind kind :path path\n                                   :key (:spell (first (first g))) :complete? (:complete? (first (first g)))\n                                   :elems (mapv second g)})))))\n\n(defn- fixpoint!\n  \"W3. Re-examine every postponed group in order under the current numbering;\n   repeat while a pass numbers a cursor cell and groups remain.\"\n  [run]\n  (loop []\n    (let [before (count @(:num run)) groups @(:groups run)]\n      (reset! (:groups run) [])\n      (doseq [{:keys [container kind elems path]} groups] (unordered! run container kind elems path))\n      (when (and (seq @(:groups run)) (> (count @(:num run)) before)) (recur)))))\n\n(defn- unnumbered-cells [run kind e]\n  (let [num @(:num run)]\n    (set (remove #(contains? num %) (item-cells (:ctx run) :V (elem-item kind e))))))\n\n(defn- group-failure\n  \"T, the tie test. nil when the group's members are interchangeable: the\n   common key is complete, and the members' unnumbered cursor cells are\n   pairwise disjoint and occur in no member of another remaining group.\n   Otherwise the reason.\"\n  [run groups g]\n  (let [own (mapv #(unnumbered-cells run (:kind g) %) (:elems g))\n        others (reduce into #{} (for [h groups :when (not= (:id h) (:id g)) e (:elems h)]\n                                  (unnumbered-cells run (:kind h) e)))]\n    (cond (not (:complete? g)) :incomplete-key\n          (not= (reduce + (map count own)) (count (reduce into #{} own))) :shared-within-group\n          (some #(seq (set/intersection % others)) own) :shared-across-groups\n          :else nil)))\n\n(defn- resolve!\n  \"Postponed groups to completion: fixpoint, then the tie test on every\n   remaining group; all pass: enter them in listed order and repeat; any\n   fails: the root run refuses, a key run leaves them as residue.\"\n  [run]\n  (loop []\n    (fixpoint! run)\n    (let [groups @(:groups run) ctx (:ctx run)]\n      (when (seq groups)\n        (let [failing (vec (keep (fn [g] (when-let [why (group-failure run groups g)] (assoc g :why why))) groups))]\n          (when (and *trace* (= :n (:tag run)))\n            (println \"  [ties]\" (mapv (fn [g] [(:id g) (:path g) (:elems g) (:why g)]) (map #(assoc % :why (group-failure run groups %)) groups))))\n          (cond\n            (empty? failing)\n            ;; Interchangeable groups are independent of each other (their\n            ;; cells are confined), so all are entered before the next pass.\n            (do (reset! (:groups run) [])\n                (doseq [g groups e (:elems g)] (enter-slot! run :V (elem-item (:kind g) e) (conj (:path g) :member)))\n                (recur))\n            (:permissive ctx)\n            ;; Diagnostic only: enter the first group in listed order, then\n            ;; re-key the rest (what an unsound \"equal keys, host order\" rule does).\n            (do (reset! (:groups run) (vec (rest groups)))\n                (doseq [e (:elems (first groups))] (enter-slot! run :V (elem-item (:kind (first groups)) e) (conj (:path (first groups)) :member)))\n                (recur))\n            (= :n (:tag run))\n            (reset! (:refused run)\n                    {:kind :unresolved-cursor-cells\n                     :path (:path (first failing))\n                     :why (mapv :why failing)\n                     :cursor-cells (vec (sort (distinct (mapcat (fn [g] (mapcat #(unnumbered-cells run (:kind g) %) (:elems g))) failing))))})\n            :else nil))))))\n\n(defn- local-run\n  \"A key walk: the same procedure on one member from the enclosing run's\n   numbering, tag :u; its result is the member's key (spelling under its\n   final numbering, residue spelled [:tie K ...]) and whether it is complete.\n   Memoized on (item, numbering restricted to the item's cells, counter).\"\n  [run item path]\n  (let [ctx (:ctx run)\n        cells (item-cells ctx :V item)\n        num @(:num run)\n        start (if (= :u (:tag run)) @(:next run) 0)\n        mk [item (select-keys num cells) start]]\n    (or (get @(:memo ctx) mk)\n        (let [sub (new-run ctx num :u start)]\n          (spend! ctx :work (count cells))\n          (enter-slot! sub :V item path)\n          (resolve! sub)\n          (let [spell (spell-slot sub :V item path)\n                r {:spell spell :bytes (key-bytes! ctx spell) :complete? (empty? @(:groups sub))}]\n            (swap! (:counter ctx) update :local-runs (fnil + 0) 1)\n            (swap! (:memo ctx) assoc mk r)\n            r)))))\n\n;; -------------------------------------------------------------- spelling\n\n(defn- spell-cell [run c]\n  (let [[t k] (get @(:num run) c) ctx (:ctx run)]\n    (case t\n      :n [:cursor-cell [:n k]]\n      :u [:cursor-cell (if (:count-spelling ctx)\n                         [:u k (get (:ranks ctx) c) (get (:counts ctx) c)]\n                         [:u k (get (:ranks ctx) c)])]\n      (throw (ex-info \"spelling an unnumbered cursor cell\" {:cursor-cell c})))))\n\n(defn- spell-slot [run d x path]\n  (spend! (:ctx run) :work 1)\n  (cond (ref? d) (spell-node run x path)\n        (refs? d) (vec (map-indexed (fn [i n] (spell-node run n (conj path i))) x))\n        (= :C d) (spell-cell run x)\n        (v? d) (if (nil? x) x\n                   (case (first x)\n                     :cursor-cell (spell-cell run (second x))\n                     :row [:row (spell-node run (second x) path)]\n                     x))\n        :else x))\n\n(defn- spell-node\n  \"The spelling of a row under the run's final numbering: literals and\n   structural data as themselves (by reference), rows expanded in place,\n   keyed rows in key order, a :set or :map as the sorted vector of its\n   members' spellings with each surviving tie group as [:tie K ...].\"\n  [run n path]\n  (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n ctx (:ctx run) ds (descriptors kind slots)]\n    (cond\n      (= :cursor-cells kind) [:cursor-cells]\n      (child-task? ctx n) [:child]\n      (= :task kind)\n      (into [kind]\n            (map-indexed (fn [i [d x]]\n                           (if (contains? #{7 12} i)\n                             (sort-by-key! ctx #(nth % 1) (mapv #(spell-node run % (conj path i (first (:slots %)))) x))\n                             (spell-slot run d x (conj path i))))\n                         (map vector ds slots)))\n      (contains? keyed-structural kind)\n      (into [kind] (mapcat identity (sort-by-key! ctx first\n                                                  (mapv (fn [[k v]] [k (spell-slot run (second ds) v (conj path k))])\n                                                        (partition 2 slots)))))\n      (= :window kind)\n      (into [kind] (mapcat (fn [[r v]] [r (spell-slot run :V v (conj path r))]) (sort-by first (partition 2 slots))))\n      (contains? #{:set :map} kind)\n      (let [elems (if (= :set kind) (vec slots) (mapv vec (partition 2 slots)))\n            tied (filter #(identical? n (:container %)) @(:groups run))\n            tied-elems (set (mapcat :elems tied))\n            plain (keep (fn [e] (when-not (tied-elems e) (spell-slot run :V (elem-item kind e) (conj path :member)))) elems)\n            ties (map #(into [:tie] (repeat (count (:elems %)) (:key %))) tied)]\n        (into [kind] (sort-by-key! ctx identity (concat plain ties))))\n      :else (into [kind] (map-indexed (fn [i [d x]] (spell-slot run d x (conj path i))) (map vector ds slots))))))\n\n;; ------------------------------------------------------------- procedure\n\n(def ^:dynamic *numbering-opts*\n  \"Options for every run of the procedure in scope (root and install\n   children): :permissive, :count-spelling, :budget.\"\n  {})\n\n(defn discovery-numbering\n  \"Returns {:numbering {src -> :yin.k/cc-n} :used {...}} or {:refused {...}}.\n   Throws :resource-limit when a budget is exceeded, and a defect (never a\n   refusal) when the numbering is not total.\"\n  ([task] (discovery-numbering task *numbering-opts*))\n  ([task opts]\n   (let [census (nth (:slots task) 9)\n         bodies (into {} (map vec) (partition 2 (:slots census)))\n         ctx {:task task :bodies bodies\n              :memo (atom {}) :cells-memo (atom {})\n              :budget (merge default-budget (:budget opts))\n              :counter (atom {})\n              :permissive (:permissive opts)\n              :count-spelling (not= false (:count-spelling opts))}\n         _ (spend! ctx :cursor-cells (count bodies))\n         ctx (assoc ctx :ranks (body-ranks ctx bodies) :counts (occurrence-counts ctx task))\n         run (new-run ctx {} :n 1)]\n     (enter-node! run task [])\n     (resolve! run)\n     (if-let [r @(:refused run)]\n       {:refused r :used @(:counter ctx)}\n       (let [numbered (set (keys @(:num run))) declared (set (keys bodies))]\n         (when (seq @(:groups run)) (throw (ex-info \"residue after resolve\" {})))\n         (when (not= numbered declared)\n           (throw (ex-info \"numbering is not total\" {:missing (vec (sort (remove numbered declared)))\n                                                      :extra (vec (sort (remove declared numbered)))})))\n         {:numbering (into {} (map (fn [[c [_ k]]] [c (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"cc-\" k))])) @(:num run))\n          :used @(:counter ctx)})))))\n\n;; --------------------------------------------------------------- emission\n;; 6a's emit-node with install children numbered by discovery order and a\n;; row path threaded for the child refusal.\n\n(def ^:private ordered-slots @#'rows/ordered-slots)\n(def ^:private check-literal-markers! @#'rows/check-literal-markers!)\n(def ^:private byte-compare @#'rows/byte-compare)\n\n(declare emit-node*)\n\n(defn- refuse-unresolved! [r path]\n  (throw (ex-info \"unresolved cursor cells\"\n                  {:yin.k/status :yin.k/non-portable :yin.k/kind :unresolved-cursor-cells\n                   :yin.k/path (into path (:path r)) :yin.k/cursor-cells (:cursor-cells r)\n                   ;; probe-only diagnostic, not part of the refusal's contract\n                   :probe/why (:why r)})))\n\n(defn- emit-slot* [d x numbering rows path]\n  (when-not (or (ref? d) (refs? d) (= :C d))\n    (check-literal-markers! (if (v? d) (when (= :lit (first x)) (second x)) x)))\n  (cond\n    (ref? d) (emit-node* x numbering rows path)\n    (refs? d) (reduce (fn [[out rs] [j n]]\n                        (let [p (conj path (if (= :install (:kind n)) (first (:slots n)) j))\n                              [id rs'] (emit-node* n numbering rs p)]\n                          [(conj out id) rs']))\n                      [[] rows] (map-indexed vector x))\n    (= d :C) [(get numbering x x) rows]\n    (v? d) (case (first x)\n             :row (let [[id rs] (emit-node* (second x) numbering rows path)] [[:row id] rs])\n             :cursor-cell [[:cursor-cell (get numbering (second x) (second x))] rows]\n             [x rows])\n    :else [x rows]))\n\n(defn- emit-node* [n numbering rows path]\n  (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n\n        [slots rows] (reduce (fn [[out rs] [i d x]]\n                               (if (and (ref? d) (= :task (:kind x)))\n                                 (let [r (discovery-numbering x)\n                                       _ (when (:refused r) (refuse-unresolved! (:refused r) path))\n                                       [id child-rows] (emit-node* x (:numbering r) {} [])]\n                                   [(conj out id) (merge rs child-rows)])\n                                 (let [[x' rs'] (emit-slot* d x numbering rs (conj path i))] [(conj out x') rs'])))\n                             [[] rows] (map vector (range) (descriptors kind slots) slots))\n        slots (if (= kind :task)\n                (-> slots\n                    (update 7 #(vec (sort (fn [a b] (byte-compare (nth (get rows a) 2) (nth (get rows b) 2))) %)))\n                    (update 12 #(vec (sort (fn [a b] (byte-compare (nth (get rows a) 2) (nth (get rows b) 2))) %))))\n                (ordered-slots kind slots))\n        body (into [kind] slots) id (jing/segment-key body)]\n    [id (assoc rows id (into [id] body))]))\n\n(defn emit*\n  \"Lift side: number by discovery order, emit; refuses :yin.k/non-portable\n   :unresolved-cursor-cells for the root or for any install child (path\n   [12 <name> ...]); a budget refusal propagates as itself.\"\n  [task]\n  (let [r (discovery-numbering task)]\n    (when (:refused r) (refuse-unresolved! (:refused r) []))\n    (let [[id rows] (emit-node* task (:numbering r) {} [])]\n      {:yin.k/handoff true :yin.k/version 3 :yin.k/root id :yin.k/rows (vec (vals rows))})))\n\n(defn decode*\n  \"Receiver side: 6a's decode* with its own numbering check off (it still\n   runs 6a's recompute under 6a's budget: a probe limitation), then the whole\n   discovery recomputation (root and install children) under one\n   translation: only a lift-side :yin.k/non-portable of kind\n   :unresolved-cursor-cells becomes :yin.k/undecodable\n   :unresolved-cursor-cells with the path prefixed by the carried root id;\n   anything else (a resource refusal) propagates as itself.\"\n  [wire]\n  (let [task (@#'rows/decode* wire (assoc rows/default-budget :check-numbering false))\n        root (:yin.k/root wire)\n        id (try (:yin.k/root (emit* task))\n                (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n                  (let [d (ex-data e)]\n                    (if (and (= :yin.k/non-portable (:yin.k/status d)) (= :unresolved-cursor-cells (:yin.k/kind d)))\n                      (throw (ex-info \"unresolved cursor cells\"\n                                      (assoc d :yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/path (into [root] (:yin.k/path d)))))\n                      (throw e)))))]\n    (when (not= id root)\n      (throw (ex-info \"noncanonical\" {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/kind :noncanonical-cursor-cells\n                                      :yin.k/path [root]})))\n    task))\n\n(defn error [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch Throwable e (or (ex-data e) {:throwable (str e)}))))\n\n(defn do-root\n  \"Root id, {:refused ...} for the tie refusal, or {:resource-limit path}.\"\n  [task]\n  (try (:yin.k/root (emit* task))\n       (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n         (let [d (ex-data e)]\n           (case (:yin.k/kind d)\n             :unresolved-cursor-cells {:refused d}\n             :resource-limit {:resource-limit (:yin.k/path d)}\n             (throw e))))))\n\n(defn safe-6a-root [task]\n  (try (:yin.k/root (rows/emit task))\n       (catch Throwable e {:refused (select-keys (ex-data e) [:yin.k/kind :yin.k/path])})))\n\n;; ------------------------------------------------------------ generators\n\n(defn rename-and-shuffle\n  \"Rename every cursor cell by `renaming` and shuffle every :set, :map and\n   the census in listed order (shuffle is rebound by callers).\"\n  [n renaming]\n  (letfn [(value [v] (case (first v)\n                       :cursor-cell [:cursor-cell (bij (second v))]\n                       :row [:row (go (second v))]\n                       v))\n          (bij [x] (get renaming x x))\n          (go [n]\n            (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n]\n              (case kind\n                :set (rows/node :set (vec (shuffle (mapv value slots))))\n                :map (rows/node :map (vec (mapcat identity (shuffle (mapv (fn [[k v]] [(value k) (value v)]) (partition 2 slots))))))\n                :cursor-cells (rows/node :cursor-cells (vec (mapcat (fn [[c b]] [(bij c) (go b)]) (shuffle (mapv vec (partition 2 slots))))))\n                (rows/node kind (mapv (fn [d x]\n                                        (cond (ref? d) (go x)\n                                              (refs? d) (mapv go x)\n                                              (= :C d) (bij x)\n                                              (v? d) (if x (value x) x)\n                                              :else x))\n                                      (descriptors kind slots) slots)))))]\n    (go n)))\n\n(defn reorder\n  \"The task with f applied to the listed members of every :set and :map, in\n   walk order (f gets the container's ordinal and its members, a map's as\n   [k v] pairs); install children included; census untouched.\"\n  [task f]\n  (let [i (atom -1)]\n    (letfn [(value [v] (case (first v) :row [:row (go (second v))] v))\n            (go [n]\n              (let [{:keys [kind slots]} n]\n                (case kind\n                  :set (let [k (swap! i inc) ms (mapv value slots)] (rows/node :set (vec (f k ms))))\n                  :map (let [k (swap! i inc) ps (mapv (fn [[a b]] [(value a) (value b)]) (partition 2 slots))]\n                         (rows/node :map (vec (mapcat identity (f k ps)))))\n                  (rows/node kind (mapv (fn [d x]\n                                          (cond (ref? d) (go x)\n                                                (refs? d) (mapv go x)\n                                                (v? d) (if x (value x) x)\n                                                :else x))\n                                        (descriptors kind slots) slots)))))]\n      (go task))))\n\n(defn all-census-cells\n  \"Source ids of every census in the tree (root and install children).\"\n  [task]\n  (let [acc (atom [])]\n    (letfn [(node [n] (when (map? n)\n                        (when (= :cursor-cells (:kind n)) (swap! acc into (take-nth 2 (:slots n))))\n                        (doseq [[d x] (map vector (descriptors (:kind n) (:slots n)) (:slots n))]\n                          (cond (ref? d) (node x) (refs? d) (run! node x)\n                                (v? d) (when (and x (= :row (first x))) (node (second x)))))))]\n      (node task) (vec @acc))))\n\n(defn seeded-shuffle [^java.util.Random r]\n  (fn [xs] (let [a (java.util.ArrayList. ^java.util.Collection (vec xs))]\n             (java.util.Collections/shuffle a r)\n             (vec a))))\n\n(defn decoded\n  \"Portable decoded equality of an abstract value (check-abstract!'s rule).\"\n  [v]\n  (case (first v)\n    :lit [:lit (second v)]\n    :cursor-cell [:identity (second v)]\n    :row (let [n (second v) ss (:slots n)]\n           (case (:kind n)\n             :vec [:seq (mapv decoded ss)]\n             :set [:set (set (map decoded ss))]\n             :map [:map (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [(decoded k) (decoded x)])) (partition 2 ss))]\n             [:row n]))))\n\n(defn distinct-decoded [vs]\n  (vec (vals (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (pr-str %1) (pr-str %2))) (map (fn [e] [(decoded e) e])) vs))))\n\n(defn gen-value\n  \"Random V over `cells`, depth-bounded: literals, cursor cells, vectors,\n   sets, maps (cursor cells as keys too), sets of cursor-cell pairs (edges,\n   aliases such as [X X] included), sets of sets.\"\n  [^java.util.Random r cells depth]\n  (let [pick (fn [xs] (nth xs (.nextInt r (count xs))))\n        cc (fn [] [:cursor-cell (pick cells)])\n        k (.nextInt r (if (pos? depth) 9 3))]\n    (case k\n      0 [:lit (pick [1 2 :k \"s\" nil])]\n      1 (cc)\n      2 (cc)\n      3 (let [elems (vec (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 3)) #(gen-value r cells (dec depth))))]\n          (if (some #(not= :lit (first %)) elems) [:row (rows/node :vec elems)] [:lit (mapv second elems)]))\n      4 (let [elems (distinct-decoded (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 4)) #(gen-value r cells (dec depth))))]\n          (if (some #(not= :lit (first %)) elems) [:row (rows/node :set elems)] [:lit (set (map second elems))]))\n      5 (let [pairs (vec (vals (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (pr-str %1) (pr-str %2))) (map (fn [p] [(decoded (first p)) p]))\n                                     (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 3)) #(vector (gen-value r cells (dec depth)) (gen-value r cells (dec depth)))))))]\n          (if (some (fn [[a b]] (or (not= :lit (first a)) (not= :lit (first b)))) pairs)\n            [:row (rows/node :map (vec (mapcat identity pairs)))]\n            [:lit (into {} (map (fn [[a b]] [(second a) (second b)])) pairs)]))\n      (6 7) (let [edges (distinct-decoded (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt r 3)) #(vector :row (rows/node :vec [(cc) (cc)]))))]\n              [:row (rows/node :set edges)])\n      8 (let [inner (distinct-decoded (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt r 2))\n                                                  #(let [es (distinct-decoded (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 3)) cc))]\n                                                     [:row (rows/node :set es)])))]\n          [:row (rows/node :set inner)]))))\n\n(defn reached [v]\n  (let [acc (atom #{})]\n    (letfn [(w [v] (case (first v)\n                     :cursor-cell (swap! acc conj (second v))\n                     :row (doseq [s (:slots (second v))] (w s))\n                     nil))]\n      (w v) @acc)))\n\n(defn gen-task\n  \"A :halted task: 1-6 cursor cells over two bodies (ties common), 1-3 store\n   bindings and the result slot hold random values.\"\n  [seed]\n  (let [r (java.util.Random. seed)\n        k (inc (.nextInt r 6))\n        cells (mapv #(keyword \"src\" (str \"c\" %)) (range k))\n        bodies (mapv (fn [_] (rt/cursor-cell-body :s (if (zero? (.nextInt r 3)) 1 0))) cells)\n        names (vec (take (inc (.nextInt r 3)) '[a b c]))\n        vals (mapv (fn [_] (gen-value r cells 3)) names)\n        result (gen-value r cells 2)\n        used (reduce into (reached result) (map reached vals))\n        census (keep (fn [[c b]] (when (used c) [c b])) (map vector cells bodies))]\n    (if (empty? used)\n      (recur (inc seed))\n      (let [t (rt/task-node census result)]\n        (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots t) 6 (rows/node :store (vec (mapcat (fn [n v] [n v]) names vals)))))))))\n\n(defn gen-incidence-task\n  \"The reviewer's tie-heavy incidence families (r3 review, seed-driven):\n   2-8 cells of one body; edge sets, overlapping groups, aliased maps,\n   repeated and nested containers, reversed edges, ordered anchors.\"\n  [seed]\n  (let [r (java.util.Random. seed)\n        sh (seeded-shuffle r)\n        c (fn [x] [:cursor-cell x])\n        v (fn [xs] [:row (rows/node :vec (vec xs))])\n        s (fn [xs] [:row (rows/node :set (distinct-decoded xs))])\n        m (fn [ps] [:row (rows/node :map (vec (mapcat identity (vals (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (pr-str %1) (pr-str %2)))\n                                                                             (map (fn [p] [(decoded (first p)) p])) ps)))))])\n        n (+ 2 (.nextInt r 7)) cs (mapv #(keyword \"src\" (str \"i\" %)) (range n))\n        cc #(c (nth cs (.nextInt r n)))\n        edge #(v [(cc) (cc)]) es (vec (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt r 9)) edge))\n        group #(s (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt r 4)) cc))\n        value (case (mod seed 10)\n                0 (s es)\n                1 (v [(s es) (s (sh es))])\n                2 (s (repeatedly 4 group))\n                3 (v [(s es) (cc)])\n                4 (s (map #(v [% (group)]) es))\n                5 (m (mapv (fn [x] [(c x) (cc)]) cs))\n                6 (v [(s es) (s (map #(v (reverse (:slots (second %)))) es))])\n                7 (s (map #(m [[(cc) %] [[:lit :anchor] (group)]]) es))\n                8 (s [(v [(s es) (group)]) (v [(group) (s (sh es))])])\n                9 (v [(s es) (s (repeatedly 4 group)) (cc)]))\n        b (rt/cursor-cell-body :s 0)]\n    (rt/task-node (mapv #(vector % b) (sort (reached value))) value)))\n\n(defn worked-act []\n  (first (:slots (rows/decode (rows/frame->rows ft/worked-frame)))))\n\n(def park-vector [[:closure 0 [] 2] [:halt 0] [:park 0] [:return 0]])\n(def park-address (jing/segment-key park-vector))\n\n(defn frame-task\n  \"A blocked task carrying the worked code plus a park segment. The wait's\n   act holds `wait-values` in its window register 1 and in one K frame's\n   window register 1; `env-value`, when given, is bound to e0 in the free\n   environment and in every environment; the parked state (P 7) is an act\n   at the park site whose K frame holds `parked-value` in register 1.\n   Decodes under 6a's validate-frames.\"\n  [census wait-values env-value parked-value]\n  (let [base (rt/task-node (conj (vec census) [:test/cursor (rt/cursor-cell-body :s 0)]) nil)\n        [seg pc env window k rd] (:slots (worked-act))\n        [_ store-of] (:slots env)\n        bindings (rows/node :bindings (if env-value ['e0 env-value] []))\n        env (rows/node :env [bindings store-of])\n        kframe (fn [v] (rows/node :kframe [seg pc env (rows/node :window [1 v]) rd]))\n        [w1 w2] wait-values\n        wait-act (rows/node :act [seg pc env (rows/node :window [1 w1]) (rows/node :k (if w2 [(kframe w2)] [])) rd])\n        pending (second (:slots (rows/decode (rows/frame->rows ft/worked-frame))))\n        parked (rows/node :act [park-address 3 env (rows/node :window []) (rows/node :k [(kframe parked-value)]) 0])]\n    (rows/node :task (-> (:slots base) (assoc 2 :blocked) (assoc 5 bindings)\n                         (assoc 11 (merge ft/worked-code {park-address park-vector}))\n                         (assoc 8 (rows/node :parked-table (if parked-value [7 parked] [])))\n                         (assoc 13 [(rows/node :wait [wait-act pending])]) (assoc 16 {:yin.k/policy :yin.k/fork})))))\n\n(defn gen-frame-task [seed]\n  (let [r (java.util.Random. seed)\n        k (inc (.nextInt r 4))\n        cells (mapv #(keyword \"src\" (str \"f\" %)) (range k))\n        body (rt/cursor-cell-body :s 0)\n        pick (fn [] (gen-value r cells 2))\n        wait-values (vec (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 2)) pick))\n        env-value (when (zero? (.nextInt r 2)) (pick))\n        parked-value (when (zero? (.nextInt r 2)) (pick))\n        used (reduce into #{} (map reached (remove nil? (concat wait-values [env-value