{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015pjw7dcte5QvkVyZs8jCYL","type":"tool_result","content":"3:Reviewed HEAD `1bb2638cfcf00e509f34bf463e3083e51d593697`, including the uncommitted note and prototype. Phase 6a reference: `d77da9f04276fca34db6fe6c36bea38a576c09b2`. Only this findings file was edited. Review ran in the foreground, without agents. JVM commands used `mise exec -- java -Xmx1g @java.args clojure.main -` from the probe directory, with scripts supplied on stdin.\n17:## Previous findings and independent reruns\n53:The independent generator was reconstructed around the prior review's ten incidence families, rather than using the author's recursive generator. Seed `179221`; 2–8 candidate cells with equal bodies; pair relations, overlapping groups, aliased maps, repeated/nested containers, reversed edges and ordered anchors. There were 250 install-child states. Each state was compared with **two independently renamed copies**, permuting every set, map and census. The renamer was implemented independently of `p/rename-and-shuffle`.\n70:## Budget evidence\n92:## D6 proof and coverage\n98:```clojure\n115:## Rank order and section 8 audit\n121:```clojure\n150:## Simplicity and recommendation\n160:## Reproducible independent generator\n164:```clojure\n166:(def rng (java.util.Random. 179221))\n183:(defn gen [i]\n---\n10:**What is refused, and why.** `#{[A B] [B A]}`: both pairs key alike and share both cells, so the test cannot prove the swap harmless (it is), and proving it would need a search; refused as `:unresolved-cursor-cells`, and a receiver that recomputes it refuses `:yin.k/undecodable` of the same kind. Same for `[#{X Y} #{X Y}]` and a few shapes like them. The seven-cell triangle plus square is refused too, and that one genuinely needs a search: entering a triangle edge first or a square edge first gives different bytes. Over generated states the refusal rate is 19 of 2000 random values, 4 of 200 frame-bearing states, 2 of 100 with install children, and 168 of 1000 of the reviewer's deliberately tie-heavy states; of all refusals, 21 were truly order-dependent and the rest were harmless ties the test could not certify.\n27:| MEDIUM: coverage paragraph wrong | §3 states the exact predicate (a surviving group fails (i) incomplete key, (ii) shared within group, (iii) shared across groups) with the reviewer's mixed-body and anchored examples as refused fixtures and the exhaustive verdicts (both interchangeable; the seven-cell state not). |\n37:- Numbered / refused: random 1981/19 (16 interchangeable-but-refused, 3 truly non-interchangeable), frame-bearing 196/4 (3/1), with children 98/2 (1/0/1 undecided), incidence families 832/168 (92/17/59 undecided). Reasons: every refusal was (ii) or (iii), none (i).\n38:- A more permissive test: host-order entry at every tie would have wrongly accepted the 21 non-interchangeable states (the justification for having a test). The round-3 component rule could recover at most 7 + 0 + 1 + 74 = 82 states (those failing only by sharing across containers). The occurrence count numbers 20 + 4 + 0 + 295 states that the literal \"body plus local index\" key would refuse; it loses none.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"704437a3-7e24-494b-ab26-b13fa72d3d40","uuid":"ab2f8642-456d-4dee-b3aa-f2f8f017238e","timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:43:40.802Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"3:Reviewed HEAD `1bb2638cfcf00e509f34bf463e3083e51d593697`, including the uncommitted note and prototype. Phase 6a reference: `d77da9f04276fca34db6fe6c36bea38a576c09b2`. Only this findings file was edited. Review ran in the foreground, without agents. JVM commands used `mise exec -- java -Xmx1g @java.args clojure.main -` from the probe directory, with scripts supplied on stdin.\n17:## Previous findings and independent reruns\n53:The independent generator was reconstructed around the prior review's ten incidence families, rather than using the author's recursive generator. Seed `179221`; 2–8 candidate cells with equal bodies; pair relations, overlapping groups, aliased maps, repeated/nested containers, reversed edges and ordered anchors. There were 250 install-child states. Each state was compared with **two independently renamed copies**, permuting every set, map and census. The renamer was implemented independently of `p/rename-and-shuffle`.\n70:## Budget evidence\n92:## D6 proof and coverage\n98:```clojure\n115:## Rank order and section 8 audit\n121:```clojure\n150:## Simplicity and recommendation\n160:## Reproducible independent generator\n164:```clojure\n166:(def rng (java.util.Random. 179221))\n183:(defn gen [i]\n---\n10:**What is refused, and why.** `#{[A B] [B A]}`: both pairs key alike and share both cells, so the test cannot prove the swap harmless (it is), and proving it would need a search; refused as `:unresolved-cursor-cells`, and a receiver that recomputes it refuses `:yin.k/undecodable` of the same kind. Same for `[#{X Y} #{X Y}]` and a few shapes like them. The seven-cell triangle plus square is refused too, and that one genuinely needs a search: entering a triangle edge first or a square edge first gives different bytes. Over generated states the refusal rate is 19 of 2000 random values, 4 of 200 frame-bearing states, 2 of 100 with install children, and 168 of 1000 of the reviewer's deliberately tie-heavy states; of all refusals, 21 were truly order-dependent and the rest were harmless ties the test could not certify.\n27:| MEDIUM: coverage paragraph wrong | §3 states the exact predicate (a surviving group fails (i) incomplete key, (ii) shared within group, (iii) shared across groups) with the reviewer's mixed-body and anchored examples as refused fixtures and the exhaustive verdicts (both interchangeable; the seven-cell state not). |\n37:- Numbered / refused: random 1981/19 (16 interchangeable-but-refused, 3 truly non-interchangeable), frame-bearing 196/4 (3/1), with children 98/2 (1/0/1 undecided), incidence families 832/168 (92/17/59 undecided). Reasons: every refusal was (ii) or (iii), none (i).\n38:- A more permissive test: host-order entry at every tie would have wrongly accepted the 21 non-interchangeable states (the justification for having a test). The round-3 component rule could recover at most 7 + 0 + 1 + 74 = 82 states (those failing only by sharing across containers). The occurrence count numbers 20 + 4 + 0 + 295 states that the literal \"body plus local index\" key would refuse; it loses none.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015pjw7dcte5QvkVyZs8jCYL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfxHSXQz5yUuGXTYyK1Ye","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011HVuSKXwevLH1YzLiV68Th","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-numbering/collab/1792210000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review-r3.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md","offset":158,"limit":80},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1480,"cache_read_input_tokens":96017,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1480},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"704437a3-7e24-494b-ab26-b13fa72d3d40","uuid":"225758b5-6164-4ea1-bc24-009fd9a7a8ec","timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:43:43.516Z","request_id":"req_011CfxHSWzC539pxnikH6eFb","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011HVuSKXwevLH1YzLiV68Th":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-numbering/collab/1792210000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review-r3.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md","offset":158,"limit":80}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011HVuSKXwevLH1YzLiV68Th","type":"tool_result","content":"158\t**Recommendation within the owner's discovery-order decision: choose D6 after the blocking fixes.** D5's structural rejection is broader than the prose admits, and rejects simple legal symmetric states that 6a handles. The small code saving does not outweigh the refusal semantics, decoder translation and coverage regression. D6 repairs that regression and passed this adversarial run, but adopt it for those concrete benefits, not on a claim of materially simpler implementation or proof. Neither variant is ready under the present accounting and proof text.\n159\t\n160\t## Reproducible independent generator\n161\t\n162\tThe following is the corrected stdin script used for the reported 5,000-state run. It uses the prototype only for schema descriptors, fixture construction, numbering/emission/decode and census collection; generation, decoded equality, shuffling and renaming are independent.\n163\t\n164\t```clojure\n165\t(require '[probe.discovery :as p] '[yin.vm.ucf.rows :as r] '[yin.vm.ucf.rows-test :as t])\n166\t(def rng (java.util.Random. 179221))\n167\t(defn sh [xs] (let [a (java.util.ArrayList. (vec xs))] (java.util.Collections/shuffle a rng) (vec a)))\n168\t(defn c [x] [:cursor-cell x])\n169\t(defn v [xs] [:row (r/node :vec (vec xs))])\n170\t(defn dv [x] (case (first x) :row (let [n (second x) ss (:slots n)] (case (:kind n) :vec (mapv dv ss) :set (set (map dv ss)) :map (into {} (map (fn [[a b]] [(dv a) (dv b)]) (partition 2 ss))))) x))\n171\t(defn s [xs] [:row (r/node :set (second (reduce (fn [[seen out] x] (let [k (dv x)] (if (contains? seen k) [seen out] [(conj seen k) (conj out x)]))) [#{} []] xs)))])\n172\t(defn m [ps] [:row (r/node :map (vec (mapcat identity ps)))])\n173\t(def b (t/cursor-cell-body :s 0))\n174\t(defn task [value] (t/task-node (mapv #(vector % b) (sort (p/reached value))) value))\n175\t(defn rename2 [n bij]\n176\t (letfn [(val2 [x] (case (first x) :cursor-cell (c (bij (second x))) :row [:row (go (second x))] x))\n177\t         (go [n] (let [ss (:slots n) k (:kind n)]\n178\t          (r/node k (case k\n179\t           :set (sh (mapv val2 ss))\n180\t           :map (vec (mapcat identity (sh (mapv (fn [[a z]] [(val2 a) (val2 z)]) (partition 2 ss)))))\n181\t           :cursor-cells (vec (mapcat identity (sh (mapv (fn [[a z]] [(bij a) (go z)]) (partition 2 ss)))))\n182\t           (mapv (fn [d x] (cond (p/ref? d) (go x) (p/refs? d) (mapv go x) (= :C d) (bij x) (p/v? d) (when x (val2 x)) :else x)) (p/descriptors k ss) ss)))))] (go n)))\n183\t(defn gen [i]\n184\t (let [n (+ 2 (.nextInt rng 7)) cs (vec (range n)) cc #(c (nth cs (.nextInt rng n)))\n185\t       edge #(v [(cc) (cc)]) es (vec (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt rng 9)) edge))\n186\t       group #(s (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt rng 4)) cc))\n187\t       value (case (mod i 10)\n188\t         0 (s es)\n189\t         1 (v [(s es) (s (sh es))])\n190\t         2 (s (repeatedly 4 group))\n191\t         3 (v [(s es) (cc)])\n192\t         4 (s (map #(v [% (group)]) es))\n193\t         5 (m (mapv (fn [x] [(c x) (cc)]) cs))\n194\t         6 (v [(s es) (s (map #(v (reverse (:slots (second %)))) es))])\n195\t         7 (s (map #(m [[(cc) %] [[:lit :anchor] (group)]]) es))\n196\t         8 (s [(v [(s es) (group)]) (v [(group) (s (sh es))])])\n197\t         9 (v [(s es) (s (repeatedly 4 group)) (cc)]))\n198\t       root (task value)]\n199\t  (if (zero? (mod i 20)) (p/with-child (t/task-node [] [:lit nil]) root) root)))\n200\t(def stats (atom {}))\n201\t(def different (atom []))\n202\t(defn norm [x] (if (keyword? x) x (if (:refused x) :refused x)))\n203\t(doseq [i (range 5000)]\n204\t (let [q (gen i) ids (p/all-census-cells q)\n205\t       copies (vec (repeatedly 2 #(rename2 q (zipmap ids (sh (mapv (fn [j] (keyword \"fresh\" (str j))) (range (count ids))))))))]\n206\t  (let [a (binding [p/*numbering-opts* {}] (p/do-root q)) z (binding [p/*numbering-opts* {:residue-search true}] (p/do-root q))] (when (and (keyword? a) (not= a z)) (swap! different conj i) (when (= 1 (count @different)) (println \"D5-D6-CHANGE\" i (pr-str q) a z))))\n207\t  (doseq [mode [false true]]\n208\t   (binding [p/*numbering-opts* {:residue-search mode}]\n209\t    (let [outcomes (mapv p/do-root (cons q copies))]\n210\t     (swap! stats update [mode (if (keyword? (first outcomes)) :numbered (norm (first outcomes)))] (fnil inc 0))\n211\t     (when-not (apply = (map norm outcomes)) (println \"MISMATCH\" i mode (pr-str q) outcomes) (throw (ex-info \"mismatch\" {})))\n212\t     (when (and (< i 100) (keyword? (first outcomes)))\n213\t       (let [e (p/error #(p/decode* (p/emit* q)))]\n214\t        (swap! stats update [mode :decode (if (nil? e) :ok (:yin.k/kind e))] (fnil inc 0))))))))\n215\t (when (zero? (mod (inc i) 1000)) (println \"PROGRESS\" (inc i))))\n216\t(println \"COUNTS\" @stats \"D5-D6-CHANGES\" (count @different))\n217\t```\n218\t\n219\tVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\n220\t\n221\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"704437a3-7e24-494b-ab26-b13fa72d3d40","uuid":"e15bb59a-1f92-4114-949a-7b438a2d0a47","timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:43:43.523Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-numbering/collab/1792210000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-review-r3.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md","content":"**Recommendation within the owner's discovery-order decision: choose D6 after the blocking fixes.** D5's structural rejection is broader than the prose admits, and rejects simple legal symmetric states that 6a handles. The small code saving does not outweigh the refusal semantics, decoder translation and coverage regression. D6 repairs that regression and passed this adversarial run, but adopt it for those concrete benefits, not on a claim of materially simpler implementation or proof. Neither variant is ready under the present accounting and proof text.\n\n## Reproducible independent generator\n\nThe following is the corrected stdin script used for the reported 5,000-state run. It uses the prototype only for schema descriptors, fixture construction, numbering/emission/decode and census collection; generation, decoded equality, shuffling and renaming are independent.\n\n```clojure\n(require '[probe.discovery :as p] '[yin.vm.ucf.rows :as r] '[yin.vm.ucf.rows-test :as t])\n(def rng (java.util.Random. 179221))\n(defn sh [xs] (let [a (java.util.ArrayList. (vec xs))] (java.util.Collections/shuffle a rng) (vec a)))\n(defn c [x] [:cursor-cell x])\n(defn v [xs] [:row (r/node :vec (vec xs))])\n(defn dv [x] (case (first x) :row (let [n (second x) ss (:slots n)] (case (:kind n) :vec (mapv dv ss) :set (set (map dv ss)) :map (into {} (map (fn [[a b]] [(dv a) (dv b)]) (partition 2 ss))))) x))\n(defn s [xs] [:row (r/node :set (second (reduce (fn [[seen out] x] (let [k (dv x)] (if (contains? seen k) [seen out] [(conj seen k) (conj out x)]))) [#{} []] xs)))])\n(defn m [ps] [:row (r/node :map (vec (mapcat identity ps)))])\n(def b (t/cursor-cell-body :s 0))\n(defn task [value] (t/task-node (mapv #(vector % b) (sort (p/reached value))) value))\n(defn rename2 [n bij]\n (letfn [(val2 [x] (case (first x) :cursor-cell (c (bij (second x))) :row [:row (go (second x))] x))\n         (go [n] (let [ss (:slots n) k (:kind n)]\n          (r/node k (case k\n           :set (sh (mapv val2 ss))\n           :map (vec (mapcat identity (sh (mapv (fn [[a z]] [(val2 a) (val2 z)]) (partition 2 ss)))))\n           :cursor-cells (vec (mapcat identity (sh (mapv (fn [[a z]] [(bij a) (go z)]) (partition 2 ss)))))\n           (mapv (fn [d x] (cond (p/ref? d) (go x) (p/refs? d) (mapv go x) (= :C d) (bij x) (p/v? d) (when x (val2 x)) :else x)) (p/descriptors k ss) ss)))))] (go n)))\n(defn gen [i]\n (let [n (+ 2 (.nextInt rng 7)) cs (vec (range n)) cc #(c (nth cs (.nextInt rng n)))\n       edge #(v [(cc) (cc)]) es (vec (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt rng 9)) edge))\n       group #(s (repeatedly (+ 2 (.nextInt rng 4)) cc))\n       value (case (mod i 10)\n         0 (s es)\n         1 (v [(s es) (s (sh es))])\n         2 (s (repeatedly 4 group))\n         3 (v [(s es) (cc)])\n         4 (s (map #(v [% (group)]) es))\n         5 (m (mapv (fn [x] [(c x) (cc)]) cs))\n         6 (v [(s es) (s (map #(v (reverse (:slots (second %)))) es))])\n         7 (s (map #(m [[(cc) %] [[:lit :anchor] (group)]]) es))\n         8 (s [(v [(s es) (group)]) (v [(group) (s (sh es))])])\n         9 (v [(s es) (s (repeatedly 4 group)) (cc)]))\n       root (task value)]\n  (if (zero? (mod i 20)) (p/with-child (t/task-node [] [:lit nil]) root) root)))\n(def stats (atom {}))\n(def different (atom []))\n(defn norm [x] (if (keyword? x) x (if (:refused x) :refused x)))\n(doseq [i (range 5000)]\n (let [q (gen i) ids (p/all-census-cells q)\n       copies (vec (repeatedly 2 #(rename2 q (zipmap ids (sh (mapv (fn [j] (keyword \"fresh\" (str j))) (range (count ids))))))))]\n  (let [a (binding [p/*numbering-opts* {}] (p/do-root q)) z (binding [p/*numbering-opts* {:residue-search true}] (p/do-root q))] (when (and (keyword? a) (not= a z)) (swap! different conj i) (when (= 1 (count @different)) (println \"D5-D6-CHANGE\" i (pr-str q) a z))))\n  (doseq [mode [false true]]\n   (binding [p/*numbering-opts* {:residue-search mode}]\n    (let [outcomes (mapv p/do-root (cons q copies))]\n     (swap! stats update [mode (if (keyword? (first outcomes)) :numbered (norm (first outcomes)))] (fnil inc 0))\n     (when-not (apply = (map norm outcomes)) (println \"MISMATCH\" i mode (pr-str q) outcomes) (throw (ex-info \"mismatch\" {})))\n     (when (and (< i 100) (keyword? (first outcomes)))\n       (let [e (p/error #(p/decode* (p/emit* q)))]\n        (swap! stats update [mode :decode (if (nil? e) :ok (:yin.k/kind e))] (fnil inc 0))))))))\n (when (zero? (mod (inc i) 1000)) (println \"PROGRESS\" (inc i))))\n(println \"COUNTS\" @stats \"D5-D6-CHANGES\" (count @different))\n```\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\n\n","numLines":64,"start