{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfxKGimoe9oAejqY97U6f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018aDuAtyg41j811KATbVcX8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-numbering/collab/1792240000000-architect-cursor-cell-numbering-revise4.report.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-12 +07\n# Report: discovery-order numbering, round 4 revised after the r4 review — claude-fable-5-1\n\n## Summary for the owner\n\nThe fourth review found no canonicality counterexample: its own 5,000-state tie-heavy generator, with two renamed and shuffled copies per state, gave 0 root or verdict mismatches, and its independent bijection check found a whole-state automorphism in every passing tie group. What it required were resource-gate and wording fixes, all applied here; the rule, the proof and every pinned root are unchanged.\nThe one serious defect was ordering: the occurrence-count scan recursed before the depth gate, so one cursor cell inside 3000 nested vectors overflowed the host stack instead of refusing `[:depth]`. The gate is now a bounded iterative scan with an explicit stack, run right after the census gate and before anything recursive; it covers rows, members, literal and structural data and the census. The 3000- and 10000-deep states and a 3000-deep literal now refuse `[:depth]` under `{:depth 3}` and under the default budget; 200 nested vectors number.\nThe representation estimator had lost 6a's early abort and took 400,012 steps on a 400,000-scalar literal under `{:work 2000}`. It is now iterative and checks its running total against the remaining budget after every node: under `{:work 2000}` the depth scan refuses at its 2001st position and the estimator is never entered; under `{:work 900000}` the scan passes and the estimator aborts after 779 steps. The note now says exactly what the charge bounds: encoded bytes and encoder nodes by a conservative abstract bound, not host heap byte for byte.\nThe probe's decoder ran 6a's frame validation before the discovery recomputation, so the ordering test proved nothing. It now runs 6a's steps 1–5 with frame validation suppressed, then the recomputation, then the root comparison, then `validate-frames`, as production will at `rows.cljc:570-578`. A wrong numbering plus a reserved-name binding decodes to `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`, the right numbering to `:reserved-name`, and the 2-cycle plus the same binding to `:unresolved-cursor-cells`.\nThe incomplete-key example was stale; the replacement is `#{#{[A B] [B C] [C A]} #{[D E] [F E] [D F]}}`: equal size, every cell occurring twice, equal incomplete keys, and the two inner sets are not isomorphic. The probe refuses it by clause (i) and classifies it exhaustively as not interchangeable, which makes the clause's necessity concrete. The termination measure is now the pair (unnumbered cells, multiset of queued member sizes) with the three phases spelled out and the distinct-members premise stated.\nRefusal figures, as the reviewer asked them stated: in their 5,000-state corpus 4,110 numbered and 890 refused; of the refused, 470 exhaustively interchangeable, 100 demonstrably non-interchangeable, 320 sampled-equal and undecided. My rerun of their script reproduces every one of those counts. The rates (0.95% of random values, 2% of frame-bearing states, 17.8% of the tie-heavy corpus) are generator rates only, not evidence of production coverage either way; small valid shapes such as the 2-cycle refuse, the accepted tradeoff of a refusal-capable carrier.\nThe reviewer's balanced-alias witness `#{[X X Y Y] [Z W Z W]}` is added to the acceptance list: one root for both enumerations, pinned `5376f133…`, the reviewer's own value. The size estimate is corrected upward (about 280 added lines, not 200) and the \"cheapest sound test\" and \"no sound test without a search\" claims are withdrawn.\n\n## What was done\n\n- `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md`: status header; §1.3 wording; §1.4 decoder order; §1.5 the three gates rewritten (census pair count first, iterative depth scan second, budget-aware estimator and the qualified accounting claim); §2 termination; §3 (i) example, the seven-cell wording, the independent-corpus table and the rate qualification; §4 the cut list (gate order, scan and estimator, test rename); §5 items 15, 16, 20, 21; appendix A (prototype description, work figures, new fixture rows, gates, decoder order, independent generator, size); appendix D.\n- `collab/numbering-probe/src/probe/discovery.clj`: `depth-scan!` and `charge-rep-bound!` (both explicit-stack, lazy element sequences, charged per position before work proportional to it); the census gate on the raw pair count before the bodies map; one `:work` unit per member keyed; `decode*` in the production order; `limit!` carries the counters as a probe diagnostic; `-main` gains the decoder-order section, the deep adversarial cases, the three estimator budgets, the balanced-alias witness and the cycle-beside-fan fixture.\n- `collab/numbering-probe/codex-gen.clj`: the reviewer's r3 generator verbatim through `gen`, D5/D6 lines removed as in their r4 rerun, plus the probe's classifier over the refused states with a separate RNG. Log `codex-gen.log`.\n- Runs (foreground, `run.log` and `codex-gen.log`): the author's 3300 states, 0 invariance failures, 0 decode failures, every pin unchanged, max `:work` 625518; the reviewer's 5000 states, 0 mismatches, 4110 / 890, classes 470 / 100 / 320, first-100 decode 60 ok / 14 at 6a's retained recompute budget / 0 other.\n\n## Codex r4 findings, status\n\n| Finding | Status |\n|---|---|\n| HIGH: occurrence scan recurses before the depth gate; 3000 nested vectors overflow under `{:depth 3}` | Fixed. `depth-scan!` runs after the census gate and before ranks, counts, memo hashing, spelling or encoding; iterative, covers literal and structural data and the census. Note §1.5, §4, §5 item 21; probe section \"depth gate before any recursive scan\": 3000 and 10000 nested vectors and a 3000-deep literal refuse `[:depth]` under `{:depth 3}`; 3000 nested vectors and a 3000-deep literal in a set refuse under the default budget; 200 nested vectors number. |\n| MEDIUM: `rep-bound` lost the `remaining` argument and early abort; 400,012 steps under `{:work 2000}` | Fixed. `charge-rep-bound!` checks the running total against the remaining `:work` after every node, explicit stack; `{:work 2000}`: refused by the scan at position 2001, estimator never entered; `{:work 900000}`: 779 estimator steps; default budget: 26516 steps. Accounting claim qualified in §1.5 (abstract bound of encoded bytes and encoder nodes, not a heap ceiling; input uncounted; preparation bounded and charged). Estimator docstring no longer says \"allocating nothing\". |\n| MEDIUM: probe decoder validates frames before the recomputation | Fixed. `decode*` suppresses 6a's `validate-frames` during steps 1–5 and runs it after the recomputation and root comparison; three carriers tested (wrong numbering, right numbering, 2-cycle, each with the reserved-name defect) give `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`, `:reserved-name`, `:unresolved-cursor-cells`. Note §1.4 and §5 item 20 require the production test against the rewritten decoder with the 2-cycle variant added. |\n| LOW: stale incomplete-key example (counts 2,2 vs 1,1,1,1) | Fixed. Replaced by the 3-cycle beside the source-and-sink orientation: equal size, equal degree, equal incomplete keys, non-isomorphic; the probe refuses it (`[15]`, incomplete key) and classifies it exhaustively as non-interchangeable. Added to §5 item 16 and appendix A. |\n| LOW: termination measure imprecise for the queue | Fixed. §2: premise (distinct members, carrier §8 step 5), measure (unnumbered cells, multiset of queued member sizes) in lexicographic order with the multiset order, three phases, each step decreases the measure or ends the walk. |\n| LOW: \"the rest were harmless ties\" overclaims | Fixed. Note §3 and appendix A carry the reviewer's table (470 / 100 / 320) with \"undecided\" defined, my rerun's identical counts, and the rates as generator rates only. This report's summary uses the same wording. |\n| Also from the review body: census gate after the bodies map; balanced-alias witness; \"cheapest sound test\"; seven-cell \"no sound test\"; size estimate | All applied: gate on the raw pair count before the map; witness pinned `5376f133…` in item 15 and appendix A; both claims withdrawn in §1.3 and §3; size corrected in appendix A. |\n\nNot changed, and why: 6a's own lift-side recursions outside the numbering procedure (`check-literal-markers!`, `check-abstract!`, `emit-node`) are unguarded 6a residuals; after the depth scan they run on data nested at most `:depth`, so the numbering slice leaves them as they are. The probe still decodes through 6a's retained recompute budget (14 of the first 100 reviewer states, 397 of my 3300 stop there); the production codec has no second recompute.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**READY** for an implementation brief, conditional on the owner's two answers in note §7 (occurrence count in the key; `:work` default 4194304). The brief should carry §4's cut list with the gate order (census pair count, depth scan, then ranks and counts), both explicit-stack traversals, the decoder insertion before `validate-frames`, and §5 items 12–22 with the new cases of items 15, 16, 20 and 21.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1657,"cache_read_input_tokens":200301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1657},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"704437a3-7e24-494b-ab26-b13fa72d3d40","uuid":"cd250ae